When they go, "Wow,"

274
00:09:41,420 --> 00:09:42,420
it's cute.

275
00:09:42,421 --> 00:09:45,190
(In perfect sync)

276
00:09:45,290 --> 00:09:46,459
It's making me happy.

277
00:09:46,460 --> 00:09:48,229
I love how the outro unfolds.

278
00:09:48,230 --> 00:09:49,459
I feel good watching it.

279
00:09:49,460 --> 00:09:51,429
I feel good after watching it.

280
00:09:51,430 --> 00:09:52,710
I'm curious about what NaiN did.

281
00:09:53,060 --> 00:09:54,069
Okay.

282
00:09:54,070 --> 00:09:55,799
One flow. Endless connection.

283
00:09:55,800 --> 00:09:57,699
Convergence. Major flow.

284
00:09:57,700 --> 00:09:59,639
She's forcing the idea that it's one flow.

285
00:09:59,640 --> 00:10:00,669
Oh, not forcing.

286
00:10:00,670 --> 00:10:01,950
(Not forcing, it's emphasizing.)

287
00:10:02,040 --> 00:10:03,269
I wonder how it flows.

288
00:10:03,270 --> 00:10:04,279
Let's go.

289
00:10:04,280 --> 00:10:05,280
(NaiN's choreography practice)

290
00:10:05,281 --> 00:10:06,740
(Focusing)

291
00:10:08,380 --> 00:10:09,609
It's Hee Su.

292
00:10:09,610 --> 00:10:11,370
I can tell it's Hee Su even in the distance.

293
00:10:11,420 --> 00:10:12,549
Are they in the back?

294
00:10:12,550 --> 00:10:13,579
Oh, they're upstairs.

295
00:10:13,580 --> 00:10:15,119
They're upstairs.

296
00:10:15,120 --> 00:10:16,366
(The intro takes place upstairs unlike BABYZOO.)

297
00:10:16,390 --> 00:10:17,819
It's fun to watch.

298
00:10:17,820 --> 00:10:19,860
They're good.

299
00:10:20,060 --> 00:10:21,060
(Smiling)

300
00:10:21,061 --> 00:10:22,260
She's cute.

301
00:10:22,360 --> 00:10:23,530
Good job, NaiN.

302
00:10:23,560 --> 00:10:25,299
(Approved)

303
00:10:25,300 --> 00:10:26,330
(Clapping)

304
00:10:26,560 --> 00:10:28,399
If I were the judge,

305
00:10:28,400 --> 00:10:29,900
the result would be different.

306
00:10:30,000 --> 00:10:31,840
There was a reason she emphasized it.

307
00:10:32,100 --> 00:10:33,399
I like the flow.

308
00:10:33,400 --> 00:10:35,369
The way she utilizes the stage.

309
00:10:35,370 --> 00:10:36,769
They start upstairs.

310
00:10:36,770 --> 00:10:39,680
Then they come downstairs to continue.

311
00:10:40,380 --> 00:10:41,709
It looks like NaiN won.

312
00:10:41,710 --> 00:10:44,750
NaiN's structure is definitely good.

313
00:10:44,980 --> 00:10:45,980
Yes!

314
00:10:46,080 --> 00:10:47,179
I can beat him.

315
00:10:47,180 --> 00:10:48,520
(Confident about winning)

316
00:10:48,690 --> 00:10:51,819
My performance has a better plot.

317
00:10:51,820 --> 00:10:54,690
More people would vote for me.

318
00:10:54,930 --> 00:10:56,159
BABYZOO versus NaiN?

319
00:10:56,160 --> 00:10:57,160
The winner is BABYZOO.

320
00:10:57,161 --> 00:10:58,299
Please.

321
00:10:58,300 --> 00:10:59,900
I'm so nervous.

322
00:11:01,230 --> 00:11:03,230
(Who is expected to win between BABYZOO and NaiN?)

323
00:11:07,240 --> 00:11:08,740
(Really?)

324
00:11:08,940 --> 00:11:10,069
Are you sure you're not mistaken?

325
00:11:10,070 --> 00:11:11,080
Yes.

326
00:11:11,780 --> 00:11:13,840
Oh, I'm so relieved.

327
00:11:13,980 --> 00:11:15,709
That's what I really wanted.

328
00:11:15,710 --> 00:11:18,019
To see my name up there.

329
00:11:18,020 --> 00:11:21,019
It felt like they approved of me.

330
00:11:21,020 --> 00:11:22,089
It felt great.

331
00:11:22,090 --> 00:11:24,160
(Happy)

332
00:11:25,020 --> 00:11:26,459
I lost. This is not good.

333
00:11:26,460 --> 00:11:27,790
I was discouraged.

334
00:11:28,190 --> 00:11:29,659
"It's okay to focus on one person from time to time."

335
00:11:29,660 --> 00:11:31,400
"Not much directing."

336
00:11:31,600 --> 00:11:33,659
"Lack of ideas or structure."

337
00:11:33,660 --> 00:11:35,170
"Nothing impressive."

338
00:11:35,870 --> 00:11:38,540
I remember things like, "Not much directing."

339
00:11:38,900 --> 00:11:41,569
Since it's 40 people performing,

340
00:11:41,570 --> 00:11:44,480
he could use more structure.

341
00:11:44,680 --> 00:11:48,150
Twenty people would've been good enough for that performance.

342
00:11:48,280 --> 00:11:50,579
In the section where the choreography changed...

343
00:11:50,580 --> 00:11:52,680
(Switching to "WHERE YOU AT" from "RUDE!")

344
00:11:52,750 --> 00:11:53,819
there was no structure to it.

345
00:11:53,820 --> 00:11:55,820
It's a bummer how they just stand there and dance.

346
00:11:56,290 --> 00:12:00,689
I didn't give much directing to it.

347
00:12:00,690 --> 00:12:03,460
I get what they mean.

348
00:12:05,160 --> 00:12:07,769
It's kind of too much to handle.

349
00:12:07,770 --> 00:12:09,800
Because I know I'm not good enough.

350
00:12:10,970 --> 00:12:12,439
(The mid-point review ends.)

351
00:12:12,440 --> 00:12:13,440
Gosh.

352
00:12:13,840 --> 00:12:17,840
If I know what my problem is, I want to fix it.

353
00:12:18,480 --> 00:12:19,979
I'm curious.

354
00:12:19,980 --> 00:12:22,709
There isn't much I could do on stage.

355
00:12:22,710 --> 00:12:24,549
There's an entrance,

356
00:12:24,550 --> 00:12:26,619
and there's something upstairs.

357
00:12:26,620 --> 00:12:28,119
It got me thinking,

358
00:12:28,120 --> 00:12:30,389
"Is my standard too low?"

359
00:12:30,390 --> 00:12:33,059
Something about the structure...

360
00:12:33,060 --> 00:12:34,589
I don't know.

361
00:12:34,590 --> 00:12:35,989
I saw many comments about it.

362
00:12:35,990 --> 00:12:37,460
(Sighing)

363
00:12:37,700 --> 00:12:39,800
I don't know what to do.

364
00:12:41,170 --> 00:12:43,100
What is wrong with me?

365
00:12:45,100 --> 00:12:46,699
It's something I must overcome.

366
00:12:46,700 --> 00:12:49,669
- Will I be able to overcome it? - Of course.

367
00:12:49,670 --> 00:12:50,840
I must overcome it.

368
00:12:53,240 --> 00:12:55,280
What can I do? It's a survival competition.

369
00:12:55,910 --> 00:12:57,879
I can't lose like this.

370
00:12:57,880 --> 00:13:00,320
Whether it's good or bad, take in all the comments.

371
00:13:00,580 --> 00:13:01,689
I tend to...

372
00:13:01,690 --> 00:13:04,389
keep going until I achieve the goal...

373
00:13:04,390 --> 00:13:05,859
once I make up my mind.

374
00:13:05,860 --> 00:13:07,359
I don't even need to sleep.

375
00:13:07,360 --> 00:13:10,290
I kept working on it without going to bed.

376
00:13:10,900 --> 00:13:12,359
- BABYZOO. - Yes?

377
00:13:12,360 --> 00:13:14,569
You didn't leave until I left.

378
00:13:14,570 --> 00:13:16,030
And you're here again.

379
00:13:16,070 --> 00:13:17,540
(He never left the Directors' Room.)

380
00:13:17,670 --> 00:13:19,099
I don't deserve to sleep.

381
00:13:19,100 --> 00:13:20,839
What do you mean?

382
00:13:20,840 --> 00:13:23,039
I must win.

383
00:13:23,040 --> 00:13:24,040
I can never accept it.

384
00:13:24,041 --> 00:13:25,239
I have to pull myself together...

385
00:13:25,240 --> 00:13:26,840
and start over.

386
00:13:26,980 --> 00:13:29,060
(The light in BABYZOO's Directors' Room remains on.)

387
00:13:29,410 --> 00:13:30,919
Is anyone here?

388
00:13:30,920 --> 00:13:32,020
(Spotting her prey)

389
00:13:32,250 --> 00:13:34,250
(Startled)

390
00:13:35,220 --> 00:13:36,619
BADA.

391
00:13:36,620 --> 00:13:37,620
When are you going home?

392
00:13:37,621 --> 00:13:40,859
I think I can turn it around today.

393
00:13:40,860 --> 00:13:42,729
He thinks he can turn it around today.

394
00:13:42,730 --> 00:13:44,130
- Show me. - I need a twist.

395
00:13:44,500 --> 00:13:47,359
To win,

396
00:13:47,360 --> 00:13:50,870
I can't help but change the current formation.

397
00:13:51,140 --> 00:13:52,669
Sorry about that.

398
00:13:52,670 --> 00:13:54,369
We'll have to change the highlight too.

399
00:13:54,370 --> 00:13:56,639
But no major changes to the choreography.

400
00:13:56,640 --> 00:13:59,179
So don't worry. Just make sure to follow my direction.

401
00:13:59,180 --> 00:14:00,180
Let's speed up.

402
00:14:00,181 --> 00:14:01,550
We don't have much time.

403
00:14:01,950 --> 00:14:04,249
(BABYZOO checks the original choreography...)

404
00:14:04,250 --> 00:14:06,080
(while practicing the new structure.)

405
00:14:08,090 --> 00:14:10,049
(The dancers make a mistake due to the change in blocking.)

406
00:14:10,050 --> 00:14:11,189
Hold on, everybody.

407
00:14:11,190 --> 00:14:12,959
You can't get "RUDE!" wrong.

408
00:14:12,960 --> 00:14:15,189
It's okay to get the new choreography wrong,

409
00:14:15,190 --> 00:14:17,229
but I don't get why you're getting the original choreography wrong.

410
00:14:17,230 --> 00:14:19,260
- Don't get it wrong. Okay? - Okay.

411
00:14:19,300 --> 00:14:21,820
(Continuous choreography mistake due to the change in blocking)

412
00:14:21,870 --> 00:14:23,469
(Moving at different times)

413
00:14:23,470 --> 00:14:25,340
Wait, why are you getting that wrong?

414
00:14:25,870 --> 00:14:28,540
Are they not paying attention?

415
00:14:28,940 --> 00:14:31,639
They've been practicing the choreography for a while,

416
00:14:31,640 --> 00:14:32,716
but they still haven't memorized it yet.

417
00:14:32,740 --> 00:14:34,549
I'm really sorry, but it makes no sense.

418
00:14:34,550 --> 00:14:35,680
Again.

419
00:14:36,150 --> 00:14:37,880
Don't get it wrong. Please.

420
00:14:38,380 --> 00:14:39,720
Please don't get it wrong.

421
00:14:39,850 --> 00:14:41,119
Please. I'm begging you.

422
00:14:41,120 --> 00:14:42,590
(Silence)

423
00:14:42,820 --> 00:14:45,059
It's different. Is 0.5 correct?

424
00:14:45,060 --> 00:14:47,459
(The dancers are confused of their positions.)

425
00:14:47,460 --> 00:14:48,730
Everyone, focus.

426
00:14:49,190 --> 00:14:51,230
(The dancers still look distracted.)

427
00:14:52,360 --> 00:14:54,700
Do you want to do this 100 times?

428
00:14:58,340 --> 00:15:00,170
(The air instantly freezes in the studio.)

429
00:15:00,470 --> 00:15:01,670
Do it again.

430
00:15:02,040 --> 00:15:03,170
It's disrespectful.

431
00:15:03,540 --> 00:15:06,880
Am I not intimidating enough?

432
00:15:07,540 --> 00:15:08,780
Let's do it again.

433
00:15:10,210 --> 00:15:12,719
(Disciplined)

434
00:15:12,720 --> 00:15:14,790
Why aren't you doing it when you can?

435
00:15:15,020 --> 00:15:16,390
Why aren't you doing it?

436
00:15:16,490 --> 00:15:17,819
I have to yell...

437
00:15:17,820 --> 00:15:20,820
to make them follow me.

438
00:15:20,990 --> 00:15:23,390
This is crazy. It's killing me.

439
00:15:24,230 --> 00:15:26,560
Seriously.

440
00:15:28,100 --> 00:15:31,770
I want to keep it fun.

441
00:15:31,940 --> 00:15:35,869
It got me thinking if I didn't have what it takes to be a director.

442
00:15:35,870 --> 00:15:37,370
I was really upset.

443
00:15:38,740 --> 00:15:39,740
Here.

444
00:15:39,741 --> 00:15:41,380
Oh, thank you.

445
00:15:41,710 --> 00:15:43,149
I know it's too hard, right?

446
00:15:43,150 --> 00:15:45,150
Sit down here.

447
00:15:45,380 --> 00:15:47,349
- This is my first... - It's your first?

448
00:15:47,350 --> 00:15:48,350
It's my first video.

449
00:15:48,390 --> 00:15:50,919
So, honestly, I'm a little scared.

450
00:15:50,920 --> 00:15:52,790
So I feel like...

451
00:15:52,890 --> 00:15:55,460
"Hey. You can do more."

452
00:15:55,760 --> 00:15:57,629
(BABYZOO had to go harsh on the dancers because he was scared.)

453
00:15:57,630 --> 00:15:58,660
Yes. So...

454
00:15:58,860 --> 00:16:00,560
I'm not angry, but...

455
00:16:00,900 --> 00:16:02,530
you know what I mean?

456
00:16:03,270 --> 00:16:05,740
I want it to be perfect and...

457
00:16:06,070 --> 00:16:08,140
BABYZOO, you are really good.

458
00:16:08,240 --> 00:16:10,740
You're a really nice teacher.

459
00:16:11,380 --> 00:16:13,080
No, I can't say...

460
00:16:15,310 --> 00:16:16,310
Trust me.

461
00:16:17,250 --> 00:16:20,480
We're all happy to join your team.

462
00:16:22,620 --> 00:16:25,259
I'm running out of time.

463
00:16:25,260 --> 00:16:26,889
Today is my only chance.

464
00:16:26,890 --> 00:16:28,160
That made me sensitive.

465
00:16:28,260 --> 00:16:29,929
For that reason,

466
00:16:29,930 --> 00:16:33,060
I should apologize to the dancers.

467
00:16:33,700 --> 00:16:36,329
A lot of things changed today.

468
00:16:36,330 --> 00:16:37,630
I'm sorry about that.

469
00:16:37,870 --> 00:16:40,700
But I seriously think the new version is better.

470
00:16:41,340 --> 00:16:43,039
I know it's confusing,

471
00:16:43,040 --> 00:16:45,240
but please memorize the changes.

472
00:16:45,580 --> 00:16:47,480
The thing about performance is,

473
00:16:48,050 --> 00:16:51,819
you can give energy...

474
00:16:51,820 --> 00:16:53,250
by pulling off your roles.

475
00:16:53,350 --> 00:16:54,720
I know it's tough,

476
00:16:54,820 --> 00:16:56,120
but please keep it up.

477
00:16:56,590 --> 00:16:58,559
Thank you.

478
00:16:58,560 --> 00:17:00,519
- Thank you. - Everyone was understanding.

479
00:17:00,520 --> 00:17:01,859
We're perfect.

480
00:17:01,860 --> 00:17:03,229
I checked every single detail...

481
00:17:03,230 --> 00:17:05,759
to prevent any mistakes.

482
00:17:05,760 --> 00:17:07,430
We didn't waste a single second.

483
00:17:07,560 --> 00:17:10,430
(Team BABYZOO is actually monitoring together.)

484
00:17:10,900 --> 00:17:12,300
Keep your hands up to the end.

485
00:17:12,740 --> 00:17:14,946
The three of you. You'll have to practice all night with me.

486
00:17:14,970 --> 00:17:15,970
(Adoring)

487
00:17:15,971 --> 00:17:17,139
Team BABYZOO.

488
00:17:17,140 --> 00:17:18,740
- Let's win! - Let's win!

489
00:17:20,840 --> 00:17:22,309
(1-on-1 Signature 400 Mission BABYZOO versus NaiN)

490
00:17:22,310 --> 00:17:24,049
Everyone, cheer up!

491
00:17:24,050 --> 00:17:25,919
- Cheer up! - Cheer up!

492
00:17:25,920 --> 00:17:26,979
Let's show them.

493
00:17:26,980 --> 00:17:28,019
Yes!

494
00:17:28,020 --> 00:17:30,649
I'm second to none when it comes to structure.

495
00:17:30,650 --> 00:17:31,660
I'm confident.

496
00:17:31,760 --> 00:17:34,630
Of course, I was bugged. She was right in front of me.

497
00:17:34,830 --> 00:17:36,959
But I need to win.

498
00:17:36,960 --> 00:17:38,829
You? You're no match for me.

499
00:17:38,830 --> 00:17:41,030
I'll put my name on the Director Credit.

500
00:17:41,330 --> 00:17:42,869
- I can't lose. - Me neither.

501
00:17:42,870 --> 00:17:43,970
I can't lose either.

502
00:17:44,570 --> 00:17:46,170
(Tension rises between two teams.)

503
00:17:46,540 --> 00:17:48,169
Don't touch me.

504
00:17:48,170 --> 00:17:49,769
- Okay. - So seniority...

505
00:17:49,770 --> 00:17:50,770
doesn't even matter anymore, does it?

506
00:17:50,771 --> 00:17:52,239
- We'll see about that. - Okay. I get it.

507
00:17:52,240 --> 00:17:53,479
I love it.

508
00:17:53,480 --> 00:17:55,249
- BABYZOO. - Jo Na In.

509
00:17:55,250 --> 00:17:56,879
- BABYZOO. - Jo Na In.

510
00:17:56,880 --> 00:17:59,249
- BABYZOO. - BABYZOO.

511
00:17:59,250 --> 00:18:01,689
- Jo Na In. - Jo Na In.

512
00:18:01,690 --> 00:18:03,420
- BABYZOO. - I can do even better.

513
00:18:04,050 --> 00:18:06,459
- Jo Na In. - Jo Na In.

514
00:18:06,460 --> 00:18:08,159
I think I have a chance.

515
00:18:08,160 --> 00:18:10,060
BABYZOO versus NaiN.

516
00:18:10,160 --> 00:18:12,360
We'll now begin their Last Run.

517
00:18:13,360 --> 00:18:16,169
BABYZOO, during this mission,

518
00:18:16,170 --> 00:18:19,769
do you think you can decide who's more superior...

519
00:18:19,770 --> 00:18:21,770
after this performance?

520
00:18:22,270 --> 00:18:24,540
Yes, I'm very confident.

521
00:18:24,840 --> 00:18:27,340
(The Last Run is all about confidence.)

522
00:18:27,480 --> 00:18:28,780
I couldn't be more confident.

523
00:18:28,880 --> 00:18:31,649
Because I lost the mid-point review,

524
00:18:31,650 --> 00:18:33,219
I changed it...

525
00:18:33,220 --> 00:18:35,349
by adding more wow factors.

526
00:18:35,350 --> 00:18:36,350
I can win.

527
00:18:36,351 --> 00:18:38,760
I'll take the Director Credit.

528
00:18:38,990 --> 00:18:40,460
Let's go!

529
00:18:40,560 --> 00:18:41,689
Let's go!

530
00:18:41,690 --> 00:18:43,389
- Yes! - Yes!

531
00:18:43,390 --> 00:18:44,829
(Team BABYZOO is filled with energy.)

532
00:18:44,830 --> 00:18:46,599
What I'm most worried about is the energy.

533
00:18:46,600 --> 00:18:48,999
We won't know until they do it, right?

534
00:18:49,000 --> 00:18:50,000
Yes, we'll have to see.

535
00:18:50,001 --> 00:18:51,869
I think a director's capability is...

536
00:18:51,870 --> 00:18:53,339
the forest.

537
00:18:53,340 --> 00:18:55,240
That'd be the highlight.

538
00:18:55,970 --> 00:18:57,339
You know what's interesting about BABYZOO?

539
00:18:57,340 --> 00:18:59,240
With his bangs down, he's a choreographer.

540
00:18:59,640 --> 00:19:01,249
With his bangs up, he becomes a battler.

541
00:19:01,250 --> 00:19:03,426
They're slightly up today, so he's a slight battler today.

542
00:19:03,450 --> 00:19:06,219
My performance will be better than NaiN's.

543
00:19:06,220 --> 00:19:09,089
I changed the choreography...

544
00:19:09,090 --> 00:19:10,090
by adding more wow factors.

545
00:19:10,091 --> 00:19:12,559
I strongly believe that I'll receive a good response.

546
00:19:12,560 --> 00:19:14,120
I'm sure I'll win.

547
00:19:14,490 --> 00:19:18,959
Now, let's begin BABYZOO's Last Run.

548
00:19:18,960 --> 00:19:20,860
