00:31:51,280 --> 00:31:55,219
I think it was a clever choice to structurally dictate...

824
00:31:55,220 --> 00:31:56,850
what to watch,

825
00:31:56,950 --> 00:31:59,860
using the lighting to guide the eyes...

826
00:31:59,920 --> 00:32:03,460
like saying, "Look right here."

827
00:32:03,860 --> 00:32:07,860
In contrast to BABYZOO, NaiN utilized...

828
00:32:08,000 --> 00:32:10,099
a wide variety of dynamic formations,

829
00:32:10,100 --> 00:32:12,199
and I thought those visual pictures were stunning...

830
00:32:12,200 --> 00:32:13,800
and brilliantly staged.

831
00:32:13,900 --> 00:32:15,669
I comfortably enjoyed...

832
00:32:15,670 --> 00:32:17,116
those diverse, "Step Up" -style visuals.

833
00:32:17,140 --> 00:32:18,240
I had a lot of fun.

834
00:32:18,340 --> 00:32:19,440
I think I'm going to win.

835
00:32:19,540 --> 00:32:20,939
Seeing the judges' reactions,

836
00:32:20,940 --> 00:32:22,410
I suddenly felt uneasy.

837
00:32:22,480 --> 00:32:23,480
NaiN.

838
00:32:23,481 --> 00:32:25,850
I think you're the smartest person in the room.

839
00:32:26,220 --> 00:32:28,279
(Thank you.)

840
00:32:28,280 --> 00:32:30,949
With the second song, when you started having the guys dance,

841
00:32:30,950 --> 00:32:33,889
it wasn't like individuals. Everybody was like one group.

842
00:32:33,890 --> 00:32:34,890
(Spotless synchronization stood out even in the pair choreography.)

843
00:32:34,891 --> 00:32:37,089
I don't want to say because you're young, that's amazing.

844
00:32:37,090 --> 00:32:38,460
I think you're just amazing.

845
00:32:38,490 --> 00:32:39,599
I choked up a little.

846
00:32:39,600 --> 00:32:42,669
He recognized my capabilities regardless of my age.

847
00:32:42,670 --> 00:32:43,970
I was really grateful.

848
00:32:44,000 --> 00:32:45,029
I'm in trouble.

849
00:32:45,030 --> 00:32:47,870
Honestly, I needed to win, so I felt pretty anxious.

850
00:32:47,900 --> 00:32:49,669
I really think she was like,

851
00:32:49,670 --> 00:32:50,770
ten out of ten.

852
00:32:51,270 --> 00:32:53,239
And in the case of BABYZOO's movements,

853
00:32:53,240 --> 00:32:56,649
while using the rhythm and energy of New Jack Swing,

854
00:32:56,650 --> 00:32:59,949
I think he interpreted the moves in a far more contemporary way.

855
00:32:59,950 --> 00:33:01,249
The reaction was so positive...

856
00:33:01,250 --> 00:33:02,590
that I believe I can win this.

857
00:33:02,620 --> 00:33:03,990
But I'm confident.

858
00:33:04,220 --> 00:33:06,390
Because I made a better piece.

859
00:33:06,890 --> 00:33:09,090
The 1-on-1 Signature 400 Mission.

860
00:33:09,190 --> 00:33:11,959
Who will be the choreographer to showcase their work...

861
00:33:11,960 --> 00:33:14,600
to the audience and put their name...

862
00:33:14,660 --> 00:33:15,830
on the credit board?

863
00:33:16,770 --> 00:33:18,570
We're revealing it now.

864
00:33:19,570 --> 00:33:23,339
- BABYZOO! - BABYZOO!

865
00:33:23,340 --> 00:33:25,069
It's definitely BABYZOO.

866
00:33:25,070 --> 00:33:27,179
NaiN had that more polished...

867
00:33:27,180 --> 00:33:28,339
and cleaner feel.

868
00:33:28,340 --> 00:33:30,980
Having the male and female dancers battle was also a masterstroke.

869
00:33:31,280 --> 00:33:33,020
BABYZOO versus NaiN.

870
00:33:33,080 --> 00:33:35,250
NaiN versus BABYZOO.

871
00:33:35,320 --> 00:33:37,849
The choreographer who will claim their name on the credit board...

872
00:33:37,850 --> 00:33:39,760
as Director is...

873
00:33:39,790 --> 00:33:41,919
I need to take the Director Credit for myself.

874
00:33:41,920 --> 00:33:42,959
I'm so confident.

875
00:33:42,960 --> 00:33:44,160
It will be mine for sure.

876
00:33:44,590 --> 00:33:45,660
The winner is...

877
00:33:45,700 --> 00:33:46,876
When is the result popping up?

878
00:33:46,900 --> 00:33:48,100
When is it popping up?

879
00:33:48,130 --> 00:33:50,000
Orange.

880
00:33:50,570 --> 00:33:51,570
I have to win.

881
00:33:51,571 --> 00:33:52,970
I'm really confident.

882
00:33:53,040 --> 00:33:56,240
The choreographer who will claim their name on the credit board...

883
00:33:56,570 --> 00:33:57,570
as Director is...

884
00:34:03,010 --> 00:34:04,480
It is BABYZOO!

885
00:34:05,010 --> 00:34:07,379
(BABYZOO wins.)

886
00:34:07,380 --> 00:34:10,249
(BABYZOO gets his name on the Director Credit.)

887
00:34:10,250 --> 00:34:11,920
(1-on-1 Signature 400 Mission)

888
00:34:12,190 --> 00:34:13,420
Great work, NaiN.

889
00:34:15,390 --> 00:34:18,930
- BABYZOO! - BABYZOO!

890
00:34:19,200 --> 00:34:20,400
We made it.

891
00:34:20,500 --> 00:34:22,300
I was so happy.

892
00:34:23,270 --> 00:34:26,169
In terms of directing ability,

893
00:34:26,170 --> 00:34:27,739
BABYZOO utilized the members...

894
00:34:27,740 --> 00:34:29,840
in such a diverse way.

895
00:34:29,940 --> 00:34:33,779
It was so powerful that it genuinely moved me.

896
00:34:33,780 --> 00:34:37,310
So I think I'll be casting my vote for BABYZOO.

897
00:34:38,210 --> 00:34:39,319
The scope...

898
00:34:39,320 --> 00:34:41,050
of BABYZOO's direction was broader.

899
00:34:42,120 --> 00:34:43,449
He dialed in every detail...

900
00:34:43,450 --> 00:34:44,749
- of the acting. - Exactly.

901
00:34:44,750 --> 00:34:48,260
So in terms of directing capability, BABYZOO seems to have the edge.

902
00:34:48,460 --> 00:34:51,159
I really think she was like, 10 out of 10.

903
00:34:51,160 --> 00:34:52,429
I think it's just unfortunate.

904
00:34:52,430 --> 00:34:54,000
He's like 11 out of 10.

905
00:34:55,630 --> 00:34:57,630
Even though it was BABYZOO's piece,

906
00:34:57,670 --> 00:35:00,840
he worked the magic of making the other characters...

907
00:35:01,000 --> 00:35:02,840
come alive even more.

908
00:35:03,270 --> 00:35:05,640
Because it was a performance...

909
00:35:05,680 --> 00:35:08,740
where the staging technique shone through the dancers' utilization,

910
00:35:08,850 --> 00:35:11,409
I have high hopes that another fantastic director...

911
00:35:11,410 --> 00:35:12,549
has been born.

912
00:35:12,550 --> 00:35:13,580
I really enjoyed it.

913
00:35:13,650 --> 00:35:15,419
I felt even better...

914
00:35:15,420 --> 00:35:17,419
because it seemed like the judges fully understood...

915
00:35:17,420 --> 00:35:19,189
everything I wanted to express.

916
00:35:19,190 --> 00:35:20,459
- BABYZOO! - BABYZOO!

917
00:35:20,460 --> 00:35:22,190
This is what I told the dancers.

918
00:35:22,490 --> 00:35:24,989
"Let's create just one scene where we look..."

919
00:35:24,990 --> 00:35:26,099
"the happiest and most joyful,"

920
00:35:26,100 --> 00:35:29,030
"making everyone who watches want to dance along."

921
00:35:29,830 --> 00:35:31,699
It was probably tough in the beginning...

922
00:35:31,700 --> 00:35:34,299
with the rocky moments and endless revisions.

923
00:35:34,300 --> 00:35:37,639
Still, they trusted me and followed my lead no matter what.

924
00:35:37,640 --> 00:35:39,979
So I want to thank them again.

925
00:35:39,980 --> 00:35:43,510
They told me, "You're the best director."

926
00:35:43,680 --> 00:35:46,350
You're a really nice teacher.

927
00:35:46,520 --> 00:35:49,020
I don't think you could have done any better than this.

928
00:35:49,220 --> 00:35:50,950
I'm so grateful and happy.

929
00:35:51,090 --> 00:35:52,359
Team BABYZOO!

930
00:35:52,360 --> 00:35:54,519
- Let's win! - It was so wonderful...

931
00:35:54,520 --> 00:35:55,829
working with those dancers.

932
00:35:55,830 --> 00:35:57,490
- Let's go! - Let's go!

933
00:35:58,900 --> 00:36:00,799
In the end, BABYZOO was the only choreographer...

934
00:36:00,800 --> 00:36:02,830
who succeeded in leaving his name on this stage...

935
00:36:03,300 --> 00:36:05,169
until the very end.

936
00:36:05,170 --> 00:36:09,670
- BABYZOO! - BABYZOO!

937
00:36:10,470 --> 00:36:12,480
- You did great. - Jo Na In!

938
00:36:12,640 --> 00:36:14,740
- Jo Na In! - Jo Na In!

939
00:36:14,940 --> 00:36:16,979
It's so disappointing. It was...

940
00:36:16,980 --> 00:36:19,280
such a back-and-forth battle all the way to the Last Run,

941
00:36:20,120 --> 00:36:23,290
so I think it came down to the slimmest margin.

942
00:36:23,920 --> 00:36:26,790
I felt so bad for the dancers.

943
00:36:26,960 --> 00:36:28,159
We prepared so hard,

944
00:36:28,160 --> 00:36:30,480
so it's a shame that we can't showcase it to the audience.

945
00:36:30,690 --> 00:36:33,659
Thinking that I should have led them better...

946
00:36:33,660 --> 00:36:35,430
brought up mixed emotions.

947
00:36:35,600 --> 00:36:37,699
I'm going to win in the next mission...

948
00:36:37,700 --> 00:36:40,399
to honor all the sweat you shed for me,

949
00:36:40,400 --> 00:36:41,869
so I hope we can keep cheering each other on...

950
00:36:41,870 --> 00:36:43,269
and just enjoy dancing together.

951
00:36:43,270 --> 00:36:44,370
- Thank you. - Good luck!

952
00:36:46,940 --> 00:36:49,849
I sincerely hope that the day will come...

953
00:36:49,850 --> 00:36:51,279
when I, too, can show my piece.

954
00:36:51,280 --> 00:36:54,780
I needed a catalyst to recharge that fierce fire inside me,

955
00:36:54,880 --> 00:36:56,489
which made me want to win...

956
00:36:56,490 --> 00:36:58,750
even more in the next mission.

957
00:37:00,360 --> 00:37:01,720
BADA versus INGYOO.

958
00:37:02,120 --> 00:37:04,589
(INGYOO's new "Smoke" performance)

959
00:37:04,590 --> 00:37:07,229
(BADA's new Like Jennie performance)

960
00:37:07,230 --> 00:37:09,929
(The result of the signature choreography takeover match)

961
00:37:09,930 --> 00:37:11,630
(INGYOO won.)

962
00:37:11,800 --> 00:37:13,499
I protected my own choreography...

963
00:37:13,500 --> 00:37:15,300
while snatching BADA's away.

964
00:37:15,640 --> 00:37:17,070
It feels great

965
00:37:17,470 --> 00:37:19,339
(Chuckling)

966
00:37:19,340 --> 00:37:22,140
BADA's mental state is probably completely shattered.

967
00:37:22,380 --> 00:37:24,426
The most crucial thing is not letting myself get swept up in it.

968
00:37:24,450 --> 00:37:27,150
Since I got the first button right just the way I wanted,

969
00:37:27,350 --> 00:37:29,850
I have to carry the momentum all the way through.

970
00:37:30,220 --> 00:37:32,189
This was the very first mission...

971
00:37:32,190 --> 00:37:34,689
where my performance was being showcased.

972
00:37:34,690 --> 00:37:36,789
But having failed to secure the credit,

973
00:37:36,790 --> 00:37:41,160
I wondered if this was really all I amounted to.

974
00:37:41,460 --> 00:37:45,000
What is it that I can show through this mission?

975
00:37:46,800 --> 00:37:49,210
Can I look at the evaluations?

976
00:37:49,840 --> 00:37:52,040
How the choreographers evaluated me.

977
00:37:52,440 --> 00:37:54,040
Could I just see the shortcomings?

978
00:37:55,680 --> 00:37:57,279
(They mostly pointed out repetitive choreography...)

979
00:37:57,280 --> 00:37:59,250
(and a lack of focal points.)

980
00:38:00,080 --> 00:38:01,150
It's shocking.

981
00:38:01,750 --> 00:38:03,020
(Punching)

982
00:38:03,190 --> 00:38:04,420
(Groaning)

983
00:38:04,620 --> 00:38:05,890
This makes me feel better.

984
00:38:06,920 --> 00:38:09,201
It's sad, but what can I do? I just have to push through.

985
00:38:09,430 --> 00:38:10,729
My biggest objective right now is...

986
00:38:10,730 --> 00:38:11,929
to thoroughly study my weaknesses,

987
00:38:11,930 --> 00:38:15,299
quickly identify what I urgently need,

988
00:38:15,300 --> 00:38:18,800
and prepare for the next battle.

989
00:38:18,870 --> 00:38:21,270
This is what makes it fun. It fuels my competitive drive.

990
00:38:21,540 --> 00:38:23,270
It's not over until it's over.

991
00:38:23,470 --> 00:38:26,940
To take the Director Credit, I really need to do this right.

992
00:38:27,480 --> 00:38:29,150
Hello!

993
00:38:29,280 --> 00:38:30,310
(Team BADA Practice Room)

994
00:38:31,010 --> 00:38:34,050
So we kicked off our first rehearsal.

995
00:38:34,520 --> 00:38:37,650
I lost my signature choreography for this round.

996
00:38:37,820 --> 00:38:39,459
Everyone, isn't this amazing?

997
00:38:39,460 --> 00:38:40,689
- Yes! - Isn't it great?

998
00:38:40,690 --> 00:38:43,230
Don't you think we can pull off an insanely cool performance?

999
00:38:43,330 --> 00:38:44,359
- Yes! - Yes!

1000
00:38:44,360 --> 00:38:46,859
So for this signature part,

1001
00:38:46,860 --> 00:38:48,800
we'll be doing INGYOO's signature choreography.

1002
00:38:49,330 --> 00:38:53,200
The dancers' expressions looked disappointed and worried.

1003
00:38:53,340 --> 00:38:57,240
So I thought I should build their trust in me.

1004
00:38:57,370 --> 00:38:58,646
(INGYOO visited Team BADA for the choreography handover.)

1005
00:38:58,670 --> 00:39:01,179
When Ingyoo was teaching,

1006
00:39:01,180 --> 00:39:02,680
I took the lead even more.

1007
00:39:02,950 --> 00:39:04,349
I think you need to step forward a bit.

1008
00:39:04,350 --> 00:39:05,479
Do you want to run it from the top once...

1009
00:39:05,480 --> 00:39:06,879
- and then listen to the track? - Okay.

1010
00:39:06,880 --> 00:39:10,149
I deliberately spoke extra loudly toward INGYOO.

1011
00:39:10,150 --> 00:39:12,120
- From the top... - Check the line change later.

1012
00:39:12,460 --> 00:39:13,890
It did get on my nerves.

1013
00:39:14,090 --> 00:39:16,390
A fire was blazing inside my mind.

1014
00:39:16,930 --> 00:39:19,559
But getting emotionally hung up on that...

1015
00:39:19,560 --> 00:39:21,829
wouldn't get me anywhere, so I figured I should do my job.

1016
00:39:21,830 --> 00:39:23,829
I wanted to memorize INGYOO's piece as fast as possible...

1017
00:39:23,830 --> 00:39:26,600
so I could teach it to my team myself.

1018
00:39:27,600 --> 00:39:29,569
So I went out of my way to step to the back...

1019
00:39:29,570 --> 00:39:30,639
and teach them more.

1020
00:39:30,640 --> 00:39:31,770
It should go right away.

1021
00:39:32,070 --> 00:39:33,439
(BADA completely took over the teaching zone.)

1022
00:39:33,440 --> 00:39:34,839
(And INGYOO watched the situation.)

1023
00:39:34,840 --> 00:39:36,810
I tried to take over the room's momentum.

1024
00:39:37,050 --> 00:39:39,850
(Before anyone realized it, BADA gained the upper hand.)

1025
00:39:40,550 --> 00:39:41,550
This is interesting.

1026
00:39:41,551 --> 00:39:42,890
(There you go!)

1027
00:39:43,490 --> 00:39:45,389
(What is going on?)

1028
00:39:45,390 --> 00:39:46,490
This is really funny.

1029
00:39:46,590 --> 00:39:49,360
I could feel BADA getting all competitive in real time.

1030
00:39:49,860 --> 00:39:50,930
Right then, I went...

1031
00:39:51,530 --> 00:39:52,799
(What?)

1032
00:39:52,800 --> 00:39:53,900
We got all fired up.

1033
00:39:54,260 --> 00:39:56,076
It sparked her competitive spirit. It was scary.

1034
00:39:56,100 --> 00:39:58,170
But even so, I thought...

1035
00:39:58,230 --> 00:40:00,469
I could beat BADA once we hit the stage.

1036
00:40:00,470 --> 00:40:03,070
The dancers are going to struggle with INGYOO's choreography.

1037
00:40:03,170 --> 00:40:05,346
Pulling off this rhythm with swagger is going to be difficult for them.

1038
00:40:05,370 --> 00:40:07,340
My choreography isn't on the easy side,

1039
00:40:07,540 --> 00:40:08,640
even if it might look it.

1040
00:40:08,940 --> 00:40:11,849
While the focal design points are set,

1041
00:40:11,850 --> 00:40:12,919
I give freedom to the movements.

1042
00:40:12,920 --> 00:40:14,180
Okay!

1043
00:40:14,520 --> 00:40:17,119
I needed a lot of dancers who could deliver that vibe,

1044
00:40:17,120 --> 00:40:18,820
so I called in WE DEM BOYZ.

1045
00:40:18,850 --> 00:40:19,960
Go!

1046
00:40:20,260 --> 00:40:21,559
They all shine brightly.

1047
00:40:21,560 --> 00:40:22,729
(INGYOO's hidden trump card: WE DEM BOYZ)

1048
00:40:22,730 --> 00:40:24,860
Having WE DEM BOYZ there was such a huge relief.

1049
00:40:24,960 --> 00:40:26,159
Say, "Oh!"

1050
00:40:26,160 --> 00:40:27,680
The pure satisfaction hit immediately.

1051
00:40:27,860 --> 00:40:29,620
It felt like doing what we were meant to do.

1052
00:40:29,870 --> 00:40:31,099
(This is it!)

1053
00:40:31,100 --> 00:40:32,369
(Completely absorbing INGYOO's signature style)

1054
00:40:32,370 --> 00:40:34,869
Taking the Director Credit with my choreography...

1055
00:40:34,870 --> 00:40:36,140
is going to be pretty tough.

1056
00:40:36,540 --> 00:40:37,669
I know it will be tough.

1057
00:40:37,670 --> 00:40:40,579
It's not my choreography, so I put a lot of thought into it.

1058
00:40:40,580 --> 00:40:43,609
If some dancers find the execution too difficult,

1059
00:40:43,610 --> 00:40:46,019
I plan to resolve it through blocking and formations,

1060
00:40:46,020 --> 00:40:47,740
so not everyone needs to perform the moves.

1061
00:40:48,120 --> 00:40:52,120
And my concept was crystal clear right from the start.

1062
00:40:52,220 --> 00:40:54,460
My concept is a runway.

1063
00:40:54,620 --> 00:40:56,660
A stable, cool performance.

1064
00:40:56,790 --> 00:40:59,499
Because the visual picture I wanted to show was so clear,

1065
00:40:59,500 --> 00:41:02,229
I even held meetings on how to direct the lighting.

1066
00:41:02,230 --> 00:41:04,469
If you want silhouette lighting tailored to the positions...

1067
00:41:04,470 --> 00:41:06,469
Also, in the process of turning the runway...

1068
00:41:06,470 --> 00:41:07,939
into a mega crew scale,

1069
00:41:07,940 --> 00:41:10,369
I tried to incorporate varied visual pictures.

1070
00:41:10,370 --> 00:41:12,580
For instance, like diagonal entrances...

1071
00:41:13,240 --> 00:41:15,639
or walking out to stage a confrontation showdown,

1072
00:41:15,640 --> 00:41:17,610
I made an effort to add twist elements.

1073
00:41:17,850 --> 00:41:18,850
And I tried...

1074
00:41:18,851 --> 00:41:22,150
to utilize plenty of props and objects.

1075
00:41:22,450 --> 00:41:24,849
All these circumstances worked in my favor.

1076
00:41:24,850 --> 00:41:26,320
So I think I can win this.

1077
00:41:26,920 --> 00:41:28,559
BADA says she's going with a runway concept.

1078
00:41:28,560 --> 00:41:29,959
But isn't this a game...

1079
00:41:29,960 --> 00:41:32,600
where you can just dress sharp and let the dance speak for itself?

1080
00:41:33,030 --> 00:41:36,069
I can pack so much into the choreography,

1081
00:41:36,070 --> 00:41:37,830
so formations aren't all that crucial to me.

1082
00:41:37,870 --> 00:41:39,510
The choreography has such great flavor...

1083
00:41:39,640 --> 00:41:42,739
that the dance alone will keep all eyes glued to the stage.

1084
00:41:42,740 --> 00:41:44,539
So I sorted out the dancers...

1085
00:41:44,540 --> 00:41:46,240
capable of pulling off my choreography.

1086
00:41:46,280 --> 00:41:49,179
Even while the other team was mapping out blockings,

1087
00:41:49,180 --> 00:41:50,609
I chose to focus...

1088
00:41:50,610 --> 00:41:52,409
and take my time drilling the choreo.

1089
00:41:52,410 --> 00:41:53,719
It looks like we need to run this a few more times.

1090
00:41:53,720 --> 00:41:55,180
(Day 4 of Choreography Practice)

1091
00:41:55,480 --> 00:41:57,390
Dance quality was my number one priority.

1092
00:41:57,920 --> 00:42:00,690
So I allocated more time to drilling the choreography.

1093
00:42:00,990 --> 00:42:02,189
Even so, there were dancers...

1094
00:42:02,190 --> 00:42:04,360
who still fell short of the required level.

1095
00:42:05,290 --> 00:42:07,770
She was someone who lacked even the fundamentals of execution.

1096
00:42:08,430 --> 00:42:11,470
She simply couldn't execute the movements at all.

1097
00:42:12,600 --> 00:42:13,969
Her learning pace...

1098
00:42:13,970 --> 00:42:16,110
was noticeably slow.

1099
00:42:16,840 --> 00:42:19,640
I'm worried about whether she can pull this off.

1100
00:42:19,740 --> 00:42:20,740
Is there a part you can't pull off?

1101
00:42:20,741 --> 00:42:22,650
I think you need to ask questions.

1102
00:42:23,080 --> 00:42:25,049
(Staring)

1103
00:42:25,050 --> 00:42:26,120
Is everything all right?

1104
00:42:27,080 --> 00:42:29,120
Flip it like this. Like turning the page of a book.

1105
00:42:29,820 --> 00:42:31,920
(Grooving)

1106
00:42:32,560 --> 00:42:33,790
What should I do?

1107
00:42:34,520 --> 00:42:36,190
She just couldn't dance.

1108
00:42:37,160 --> 00:42:38,530
I look like a stick.

1109
00:42:38,760 --> 00:42:39,959
- You're like a stick? - Yes.

1110
00:42:39,960 --> 00:42:41,359
I look like a stick.

1111
00:42:41,360 --> 00:42:42,520
Keep at it and you'll get it.

1112
00:42:43,330 --> 00:42:44,499
(Stiff)

1113
00:42:44,500 --> 00:42:45,500
Yes. Like that.

1114
00:42:45,501 --> 00:42:47,600
Even after giving her one-on-one tutoring,

1115
00:42:48,440 --> 00:42:50,270
correcting the moves seems tough,

1116
00:42:50,470 --> 00:42:51,870
so I'm a bit concerned.

1117
00:42:52,040 --> 00:42:54,540
A few of the dancers were looking hopeless.

1118
00:42:55,580 --> 00:42:57,849
I've never prepared a performance...

1119
00:42:57,850 --> 00:42:59,520
with dancers like this before,

1120
00:42:59,820 --> 00:43:03,150
so I'm not sure I can put this on stage. This is serious.

1121
00:43:03,820 --> 00:43:05,919
You two, please step forward.

1122
00:43:05,920 --> 00:43:07,859
(INGYOO calls out specific dancers.)

1123
00:43:07,860 --> 00:43:08,989
(Esma)

1124
00:43:08,990 --> 00:43:10,630
(Among them, Esma is called out as well.)

1125
00:43:10,690 --> 00:43:14,160
The dancers I just picked are going to hold the cloth.

1126
00:43:14,600 --> 00:43:16,470
You'll be holding a red sheet of cloth.

1127
00:43:16,770 --> 00:43:18,569
It was my own strategy.

1128
00:43:18,570 --> 00:43:21,540
Keeping the dancers who can't pull off the moves out of sight.

1129
00:43:22,300 --> 00:43:24,169
(Immediately starting practice for raising the cloth)

1130
00:43:24,170 --> 00:43:25,269
Seven, eight.

1131
00:43:25,270 --> 00:43:26,640
Two, three, four.

1132
00:43:26,840 --> 00:43:28,980
(In the middle of practice, Esma suddenly sits down.)

1133
00:43:29,850 --> 00:43:30,910
What was that?

1134
00:43:31,150 --> 00:43:33,080
She suddenly sat on the floor.

1135
00:43:33,450 --> 00:43:36,190
(Refusing to budge)

1136
00:43:36,320 --> 00:43:37,720
Cool.

1137
00:43:40,760 --> 00:43:41,760
(Dropping her head)

1138
00:43:42,620 --> 00:43:43,860
(He spotted her.)

1139
00:43:43,930 --> 00:43:44,990
What's wrong?

1140
00:43:46,300 --> 00:43:47,330
What is it?

1141
00:43:48,060 --> 00:43:49,729
(Flustered)

1142
00:43:49,730 --> 00:43:53,770
(Tension suddenly envelops the practice room.)

1143
00:43:54,000 --> 00:43:55,469
She says she wants to know if she has...

1144
00:43:55,470 --> 00:43:56,669
- any more choreo parts. - What?

1145
00:43:56,670 --> 00:43:57,769
I don't want to know.

1146
00:43:57,770 --> 00:43:59,439
(I don't want to know.)

1147
00:43:59,440 --> 00:44:00,740
Oh, my goodness.

1148
00:44:01,180 --> 00:44:02,280
Are you good?

1149
00:44:02,480 --> 00:44:05,110
(In the end)

1150
00:44:05,480 --> 00:44:07,549
(Esma storms out of the practice room.)

1151
00:44:07,550 --> 00:44:08,950
Okay.

1152
00:44:09,320 --> 00:44:10,650
Let's take a short break.

1153
00:44:12,120 --> 00:44:13,219
What was that?

1154
00:44:13,220 --> 00:44:14,860
What? What's wrong?

1155
00:44:15,260 --> 00:44:16,489
They are...

1156
00:44:16,490 --> 00:44:19,290
questioning why they aren't in the actual dance parts.

1157
00:44:19,460 --> 00:44:21,159
I'm doing this...

1158
00:44:21,160 --> 00:44:23,106
because I want to give everyone as much of a role as possible, too.

1159
00:44:23,130 --> 00:44:25,029
I can't cater to every single one of them.

1160
00:44:25,030 --> 00:44:28,469
That sounds like some utopian, politically correct fantasy.

1161
00:44:28,470 --> 00:44:30,639
I'm sorry, but this is a survival show.

1162
00:44:30,640 --> 00:44:31,640
It doesn't make sense.

1163
00:44:31,641 --> 00:44:34,779
This is a competition where I must put skilled dancers front...

1164
00:44:34,780 --> 00:44:37,310
to grab the spotlight if I want to win.

1165
00:44:37,450 --> 00:44:39,150
I made the choice I had to make.

1166
00:44:40,180 --> 00:44:43,749
- I have something I'd like to ask. - Okay.

1167
00:44:43,750 --> 00:44:46,189
I want to hear what my issue was...

1168
00:44:46,190 --> 00:44:48,320
and what I was lacking.

1169
00:44:48,720 --> 00:44:51,930
(During the twerking part audition held today)

1170
00:44:52,060 --> 00:44:54,829
These are the selected dancers.

1171
00:44:54,830 --> 00:44:55,830
Thank you.

1172
00:44:55,831 --> 00:44:57,800
(Esma was left unpicked.)

1173
00:44:57,970 --> 00:45:00,099
I wanted to pick dancers with stable execution,

1174
00:45:00,100 --> 00:45:02,200
but you kept rushing the tempo.

1175
00:45:02,340 --> 00:45:03,639
- We only practiced for 15 minutes. - I know.

1176
00:45:03,640 --> 00:45:06,679
- And since I was in the back... - I know.

1177
00:45:06,680 --> 00:45:07,879
- I can't nail it right away. - I know.

1178
00:45:07,880 --> 00:45:09,139
I need practice.

1179
00:45:09,140 --> 00:45:10,409
The actual performance is coming up soon.

1180
00:45:10,410 --> 00:45:12,780
So I wanted to pick dancers who wouldn't mess up.

1181
00:45:12,980 --> 00:45:14,449
I won't mess up.

1182
00:45:14,450 --> 00:45:17,419
But there are too many dancers here for me...

1183
00:45:17,420 --> 00:45:19,460
to accommodate everyone's personal circumstances.

1184
00:45:19,590 --> 00:45:21,659
I have to look out for the other dancers as well.

1185
00:45:21,660 --> 00:45:22,929
There's barely any time left.

1186
00:45:22,930 --> 00:45:24,850
I needed someone I could lock in with certainty.

1187
00:45:24,890 --> 00:45:26,610
This isn't just a show. It's a competition.

1188
00:45:27,230 --> 00:45:29,390
If I don't do this right, I get eliminated right away.

1189
00:45:31,530 --> 00:45:32,800
That's why.

1190
00:45:33,700 --> 00:45:34,870
It can't be helped.

1191
00:45:35,000 --> 00:45:37,840
I'm sorry, but it is what it is.

1192
00:45:38,140 --> 00:45:41,380
It breaks my heart too. I have to cut off many people here.

1193
00:45:41,840 --> 00:45:43,749
Every time I see them watching me from behind,

1194
00:45:43,750 --> 00:45:44,910
it tears me apart.

1195
00:45:45,850 --> 00:45:48,980
They have to dance. They have to do something too.

1196
00:45:49,320 --> 00:45:52,290
I felt sorry for the dancers.

1197
00:45:52,520 --> 00:45:55,160
They must've expected to perform on stage.

1198
00:45:55,990 --> 00:45:58,030
I'd appreciate it if you understand how I feel.

1199
00:45:59,530 --> 00:46:01,729
I understand how you feel.

1200
00:46:01,730 --> 00:46:04,129
You must feel hurt and disappointed.

1201
00:46:04,130 --> 00:46:05,170
But...

1202
00:46:06,540 --> 00:46:08,599
I hope you will keep your spirits up.

1203
00:46:08,600 --> 00:46:10,470
(INGYOO offers a handshake.)

1204
00:46:10,770 --> 00:46:13,780
How can I neglect her when we're in it together?

1205
00:46:15,940 --> 00:46:17,280
We have to go together.

1206
00:46:18,980 --> 00:46:20,749
I want you to try harder tomorrow...

1207
00:46:20,750 --> 00:46:22,220
and perform well on stage.

1208
00:46:22,580 --> 00:46:25,389
As a director, I need to accept them and lead them.

1209
00:46:25,390 --> 00:46:27,160
It's what a director must do.

1210
00:46:27,920 --> 00:46:28,920
I'm curious about BADA.

1211
00:46:28,921 --> 00:46:30,606
(1-on-1 Signature 400 Mission Interim Review Day)

1212
00:46:30,630 --> 00:46:32,389
"1-on-1 Signature 400 Mission practice video."

1213
00:46:32,390 --> 00:46:34,559
"Please predict the winner of each matchup..."

1214
00:46:34,560 --> 00:46:35,959
"and who the winning director will be."

1215
00:46:35,960 --> 00:46:37,269
Oh, my gosh!

1216
00:46:37,270 --> 00:46:38,569
(Here it is.)

1217
00:46:38,570 --> 00:46:39,799
I'm already excited.

1218
00:46:39,800 --> 00:46:43,239
It's such a big match that I can't possibly predict...

1219
00:46:43,240 --> 00:46:44,569
who's going to win.

1220
00:46:44,570 --> 00:46:45,739
Should I watch it?

1221
00:46:45,740 --> 00:46:46,940
Can't wait to watch it.

1222
00:46:47,740 --> 00:46:48,940
Gosh.

1223
00:46:49,180 --> 00:46:50,610
I love it.

1224
00:46:51,310 --> 00:46:53,049
Vata is too good.

1225
00:46:53,050 --> 00:46:54,780
This is unfair.

1226
00:46:55,280 --> 00:46:56,949
He's too good.

1227
00:46:56,950 --> 00:46:58,250
(Vata is on another level.)

1228
00:46:58,550 --> 00:46:59,860
There it is.

1229
00:47:00,020 --> 00:47:01,796
(Signature choreography part in "like JENNIE")

1230
00:47:01,820 --> 00:47:03,390
(In sync)

1231
00:47:03,690 --> 00:47:06,060
Staying true to the original.

1232
00:47:06,130 --> 00:47:09,359
It's fun that INGYOO not Jennie, is in the center,

1233
00:47:09,360 --> 00:47:10,930
when it's "like JENNIE."

1234
00:47:11,170 --> 00:47:12,530
(Clapping)

1235
00:47:12,800 --> 00:47:14,869
He's too good. This is unfair.

1236
00:47:14,870 --> 00:47:16,769
His dance is too good.

1237
00:47:16,770 --> 00:47:18,539
I think he really captured the appeal...

1238
00:47:18,540 --> 00:47:21,179
and energy of a mega crew.

1239
00:47:21,180 --> 00:47:22,679
BADA!

1240
00:47:22,680 --> 00:47:24,349
Additional casting. Goodness.

1241
00:47:24,350 --> 00:47:25,350
Audrey?

1242
00:47:25,351 --> 00:47:26,880
Is this Audrey that Audrey?

1243
00:47:26,920 --> 00:47:29,149
(Team BADA's key dancer is Audrey.)

1244
00:47:29,150 --> 00:47:31,090
JAM REPUBLIC's Audrey.

1245
00:47:31,150 --> 00:47:32,790
(JAM REPUBLIC's standout youngest member)

1246
00:47:35,360 --> 00:47:36,789
Audrey is unbelievable.

1247
00:47:36,790 --> 00:47:38,359
How did she get her? I'm surprised.

1248
00:47:38,360 --> 00:47:39,360
Scary.

1249
00:47:39,361 --> 00:47:42,459
The synopsis was a runway featuring people of various nationalities.

1250
00:47:42,460 --> 00:47:44,569
I wonder how she interpreted it. It must have been challenging.

1251
00:47:44,570 --> 00:47:45,769
To carry that concept all the way through.

1252
00:47:45,770 --> 00:47:47,269
I bet BADA really brought her A-game.

1253
00:47:47,270 --> 00:47:49,546
I’m going to prove I can pull off a mega crew performance.

1254
00:47:49,570 --> 00:47:50,570
Let's see.

1255
00:47:50,740 --> 00:47:53,979
They’re coming out strong from the start.

1256
00:47:53,980 --> 00:47:55,639
They are using a lot of props.

1257
00:47:55,640 --> 00:47:57,509
The one in blue is so good.

1258
00:47:57,510 --> 00:47:58,580
It's Audrey.

1259
00:47:58,780 --> 00:48:00,480
Audrey is really carrying the team.

1260
00:48:01,450 --> 00:48:03,249
Ay!

1261
00:48:03,250 --> 00:48:04,919
The choreography is superb.

1262
00:48:04,920 --> 00:48:06,459
BADA's strength is...

1263
00:48:06,460 --> 00:48:07,959
choreography.

1264
00:48:07,960 --> 00:48:09,929
I think she composed it well,

1265
00:48:09,930 --> 00:48:11,529
in her style.

1266
00:48:11,530 --> 00:48:14,099
Then the smoke came out with a whoosh.

1267
00:48:14,100 --> 00:48:17,229
It matched the sound so perfectly.

1268
00:48:17,230 --> 00:48:18,269
It was like magic.

1269
00:48:18,270 --> 00:48:19,839
Gosh, BADA.

1270
00:48:19,840 --> 00:48:21,799
She clearly used the dancers...

1271
00:48:21,800 --> 00:48:24,069
to build these visual formations.

1272
00:48:24,070 --> 00:48:25,169
But it still feels...

1273
00:48:25,170 --> 00:48:26,740
a little unpolished.

1274
00:48:26,840 --> 00:48:28,639
There’s a lot of moving in and out.

1275
00:48:28,640 --> 00:48:31,349
It feels a little chaotic.

1276
00:48:31,350 --> 00:48:32,749
They're the opposite.

1277
00:48:32,750 --> 00:48:36,219
BADA put emphasis on the overall composition.

1278
00:48:36,220 --> 00:48:38,589
INGYOO's performance is all about being wild.

1279
00:48:38,590 --> 00:48:41,560
I think it's about the difference in their strategies.

1280
00:48:41,590 --> 00:48:42,619
I can't see it.

1281
00:48:42,620 --> 00:48:44,929
Even if it's still a bit rough,

1282
00:48:44,930 --> 00:48:46,929
I hope they will look at the artistry of it...

1283
00:48:46,930 --> 00:48:49,359
or the varied composition.

1284
00:48:49,360 --> 00:48:50,929
At the end of the day,

1285
00:48:50,930 --> 00:48:52,329
my dance has so much appeal,

1286
00:48:52,330 --> 00:48:53,640
so I think I will win.

1287
00:48:53,800 --> 00:48:55,599
It's hard to tell.

1288
00:48:55,600 --> 00:48:57,960
(BADA versus INGYOO. Which director is most likely to win?)

1289
00:48:58,570 --> 00:48:59,980
Gosh.

1290
00:49:04,080 --> 00:49:06,180
Yes!

1291
00:49:06,320 --> 00:49:07,920
It felt so good.

1292
00:49:08,250 --> 00:49:10,220
I was very sad.

1293
00:49:13,860 --> 00:49:15,460
Why am I here?

1294
00:49:16,590 --> 00:49:19,490
I had my choreography stolen already.

1295
00:49:19,660 --> 00:49:22,059
Hearing that assessment,

1296
00:49:22,060 --> 00:49:24,500
I felt like I've been pushed out into the middle of nowhere.

1297
00:49:26,070 --> 00:49:28,940
(Laughing)

1298
00:49:29,140 --> 00:49:30,769
BADA can't laugh.

1299
00:49:30,770 --> 00:49:31,770
(Laughing)

1300
00:49:31,771 --> 00:49:33,239
It must be frustrating...

1301
00:49:33,240 --> 00:49:35,480
and very painful.

1302
00:49:36,040 --> 00:49:37,250
This is hard.

1303
00:49:37,850 --> 00:49:41,380
At this point, there's no turning back.

1304
00:49:41,620 --> 00:49:44,449
She could add to it, but...

1305
00:49:44,450 --> 00:49:47,890
I don't know. Will it be able to turn out well?

1306
00:49:48,120 --> 00:49:49,890
I think it will be very tough.

1307
00:49:53,060 --> 00:49:54,540
Don't tell me everyone picked INGYOO.

1308
00:49:55,300 --> 00:49:57,030
(INGYOO)

1309
00:49:57,200 --> 00:49:58,300
No way.

1310
00:49:58,800 --> 00:50:00,839
I didn't think it would be so extreme.

1311
00:50:00,840 --> 00:50:03,570
I expected to get at least two votes.

1312
00:50:03,970 --> 00:50:05,439
This happened on "Street Woman Fighter 2" too.

1313
00:50:05,440 --> 00:50:07,580
I started getting very anxious.

1314
00:50:07,880 --> 00:50:10,479
"The overall composition and quality are not good enough."

1315
00:50:10,480 --> 00:50:12,609
"The intent of the synopsis doesn't come through clearly."

1316
00:50:12,610 --> 00:50:15,049
Because the dancers aren't moving in sync as they move in and out,

1317
00:50:15,050 --> 00:50:16,920
it feels a little distracting.

1318
00:50:17,450 --> 00:50:20,519
The comments were not something I expected.

1319
00:50:20,520 --> 00:50:22,989
It made me think about how I should fix it.

1320
00:50:22,990 --> 00:50:24,529
I felt a bit lost.

1321
00:50:24,530 --> 00:50:26,599
You know that first judgement.

1322
00:50:26,600 --> 00:50:29,129
There's someone who doesn't come across as a director.

1323
00:50:29,130 --> 00:50:31,569
It felt as if that was becoming true,

1324
00:50:31,570 --> 00:50:33,030
and I was scared.

1325
00:50:33,700 --> 00:50:36,140
The rehearsal began. Please focus.

1326
00:50:36,410 --> 00:50:37,569
He's INGYOO?

1327
00:50:37,570 --> 00:50:39,779
Yes.

1328
00:50:39,780 --> 00:50:42,040
No, it's my first time to see him without the glasses.

1329
00:50:42,540 --> 00:50:44,550
We'll run "Smoke" using vocal counts.

1330
00:50:45,150 --> 00:50:46,696
(INGYOO stole BADA's signature "Smoke.")

1331
00:50:46,720 --> 00:50:48,949
BADA must be sad. He stole it from her.

1332
00:50:48,950 --> 00:50:51,220
(He had fun making it, but he succeeded to steal it.)

1333
00:50:53,890 --> 00:50:56,190
It's perfectly INGYOO's vibe.

1334
00:50:56,260 --> 00:50:57,789
He has a really good sense of rhythm.

1335
00:50:57,790 --> 00:51:00,830
He interpreted "Smoke" with such tight, punchy movements.

1336
00:51:00,960 --> 00:51:02,430
He choreographed it so well.

1337
00:51:03,200 --> 00:51:05,869
The stage concept is raiders in a wasteland.

1338
00:51:05,870 --> 00:51:08,069
It has this Mad Max vibe where things get increasingly brutal...

1339
00:51:08,070 --> 00:51:09,669
until it ends in death.

1340
00:51:09,670 --> 00:51:12,169
INGYOO I see...

1341
00:51:12,170 --> 00:51:14,039
gets completely immersed in the dance...

1342
00:51:14,040 --> 00:51:16,549
through that vibe and emotion.

1343
00:51:16,550 --> 00:51:19,649
But I don't think storytelling is one of his strengths.

1344
