and cheered and supported it.

2145
01:21:45,840 --> 01:21:47,509
It was a dream come true.

2146
01:21:47,510 --> 01:21:49,009
I'm so honored to have been able to perform.

2147
01:21:49,010 --> 01:21:50,010
I was grateful.

2148
01:21:50,140 --> 01:21:53,510
I'll soon take the director title.

2149
01:21:53,810 --> 01:21:56,420
I'll keep going. The mega crew mission was so fierce.

2150
01:21:57,250 --> 01:21:58,520
Please!

2151
01:21:58,720 --> 01:21:59,950
What is it now?

2152
01:22:00,490 --> 01:22:02,590
What on earth is that?

2153
01:22:03,520 --> 01:22:04,590
What is it?

2154
01:22:05,230 --> 01:22:06,990
Gosh, hold on.

2155
01:22:07,530 --> 01:22:08,600
What's that?

2156
01:22:09,060 --> 01:22:10,100
What's this?

2157
01:22:10,330 --> 01:22:11,459
This... Hold on, NaiN.

2158
01:22:11,460 --> 01:22:13,230
We're the mannequins this time.

2159
01:22:14,300 --> 01:22:15,569
This is crazy.

2160
01:22:15,570 --> 01:22:17,370
There were exactly ten.

2161
01:22:17,640 --> 01:22:21,040
I saw the mannequins with our names.

2162
01:22:21,410 --> 01:22:22,480
A dancer?

2163
01:22:22,540 --> 01:22:24,080
Wait, a dancer?

2164
01:22:25,010 --> 01:22:26,010
Wait.

2165
01:22:26,050 --> 01:22:27,209
It says "choreographer" in front.

2166
01:22:27,210 --> 01:22:28,319
(It's written "choreographer" in front of the bib.)

2167
01:22:28,320 --> 01:22:29,349
Hold on.

2168
01:22:29,350 --> 01:22:32,196
You're right. The back says "dancer" and the front says "choreographer."

2169
01:22:32,220 --> 01:22:33,920
It said "dancer" behind...

2170
01:22:34,120 --> 01:22:35,790
and "choreographer" in front.

2171
01:22:35,890 --> 01:22:37,260
You can rip it.

2172
01:22:37,390 --> 01:22:39,389
You're right. Does it mean we could become...

2173
01:22:39,390 --> 01:22:41,030
either a dancer or a choreographer?

2174
01:22:41,190 --> 01:22:43,499
The name tags were made of Velcro so you could remove them.

2175
01:22:43,500 --> 01:22:45,769
Anyway, the roles will be split up among the ten of us.

2176
01:22:45,770 --> 01:22:48,199
Who will become the director?

2177
01:22:48,200 --> 01:22:50,770
And who will become just dancers?

2178
01:22:51,170 --> 01:22:53,370
This is the directors' version of Class Mission.

2179
01:22:53,540 --> 01:22:54,669
I'm scared.

2180
01:22:54,670 --> 01:22:56,310
Among us?

2181
01:22:57,240 --> 01:23:00,349
These directors will become dancers?

2182
01:23:00,350 --> 01:23:02,220
I want to become the director, of course.

2183
01:23:02,420 --> 01:23:04,020
They're top talents.

2184
01:23:04,220 --> 01:23:06,850
When else would I be able to direct them?

2185
01:23:06,990 --> 01:23:08,360
I must become the director.

2186
01:23:08,620 --> 01:23:10,619
As someone who directs others,

2187
01:23:10,620 --> 01:23:13,160
I don't think I can stand being directed.

2188
01:23:13,490 --> 01:23:16,629
It's been way too long since I was directed.

2189
01:23:16,630 --> 01:23:18,406
If I can't become a director, I need to go home.

2190
01:23:18,430 --> 01:23:20,469
I'm not exactly early in my career.

2191
01:23:20,470 --> 01:23:22,969
It'll hurt my pride if I become a dancer.

2192
01:23:22,970 --> 01:23:24,050
I should become a director.

2193
01:23:24,100 --> 01:23:25,740
- A director. - I must become a director.

2194
01:23:25,970 --> 01:23:27,640
I don't just want to dance.

2195
01:23:27,810 --> 01:23:29,139
It's not a dancers' survival show.

2196
01:23:29,140 --> 01:23:31,209
I must do my best as a director.

2197
01:23:31,210 --> 01:23:33,050
This is a directors' survival show, after all.

2198
01:23:33,410 --> 01:23:36,150
To get your name on the Director Credit,

2199
01:23:36,550 --> 01:23:39,249
you must prove your worth once again.

2200
01:23:39,250 --> 01:23:41,520
The second mission of...

2201
01:23:41,650 --> 01:23:43,320
Street World Fighter: Directors' War.

2202
01:23:43,620 --> 01:23:45,430
How will they choose a director?

2203
01:23:45,530 --> 01:23:47,559
It's completely veiled.

2204
01:23:47,560 --> 01:23:48,560
It is...

2205
01:23:48,830 --> 01:23:51,330
the Title Sequence Film Mission.

2206
01:23:51,460 --> 01:23:53,100
(Title Sequence Film Mission)

2207
01:23:53,300 --> 01:23:54,370
What is it?

2208
01:23:54,470 --> 01:23:55,470
What?

2209
01:23:55,471 --> 01:23:57,770
Isn't this the film they play when the show starts?

2210
01:23:58,370 --> 01:24:02,180
The one minute given to make an impression of the show.

2211
01:24:02,410 --> 01:24:06,050
It captures the identity of the show.

2212
01:24:06,150 --> 01:24:08,749
This mission will evaluate your sense...

2213
01:24:08,750 --> 01:24:10,820
as a film director.

2214
01:24:11,150 --> 01:24:13,189
That's good. I like making films.

2215
01:24:13,190 --> 01:24:14,649
I've worked on it a few times.

2216
01:24:14,650 --> 01:24:15,959
I was confident.

2217
01:24:15,960 --> 01:24:18,219
Anything is possible with a film.

2218
01:24:18,220 --> 01:24:21,830
I'm a bit better at it, and I like it too.

2219
01:24:21,860 --> 01:24:23,060
What you think about...

2220
01:24:23,160 --> 01:24:25,499
Street World Fighter: Directors' War.

2221
01:24:25,500 --> 01:24:27,999
Its universe, the choreographers' characters,

2222
01:24:28,000 --> 01:24:30,099
the film's tone and framing,

2223
01:24:30,100 --> 01:24:32,709
and your sense as a director.

2224
01:24:32,710 --> 01:24:34,769
You must capture all of these in one video.

2225
01:24:34,770 --> 01:24:36,079
That's the difficult part.

2226
01:24:36,080 --> 01:24:40,149
How will you capture the charm of these ten choreographers...

2227
01:24:40,150 --> 01:24:42,750
and convey it directly?

2228
01:24:43,020 --> 01:24:45,019
Those who watch the show...

2229
01:24:45,020 --> 01:24:46,289
The ones who watch the show are the viewers.

2230
01:24:46,290 --> 01:24:47,290
No matter who watches,

2231
01:24:47,291 --> 01:24:49,589
I wan them to be able to say, "That was incredible."

2232
01:24:49,590 --> 01:24:50,719
The intention of the opening.

2233
01:24:50,720 --> 01:24:53,429
I think that has to be expressed well.

2234
01:24:53,430 --> 01:24:56,159
Who will make the face of this show?

2235
01:24:56,160 --> 01:24:57,799
- Gosh. - Gosh.

2236
01:24:57,800 --> 01:24:58,929
The ten choreographers...

2237
01:24:58,930 --> 01:25:01,769
will create film draft videos.

2238
01:25:01,770 --> 01:25:03,339
We'll be filming the title draft.

2239
01:25:03,340 --> 01:25:05,610
Through those draft videos,

2240
01:25:05,640 --> 01:25:07,869
the director who will lead the Title Sequence Film Mission...

2241
01:25:07,870 --> 01:25:09,639
will be decided.

2242
01:25:09,640 --> 01:25:11,379
Thus, this mission...

2243
01:25:11,380 --> 01:25:12,949
will consist of just one director...

2244
01:25:12,950 --> 01:25:15,449
and nine choreographers...

2245
01:25:15,450 --> 01:25:17,650
who will work under that director.

2246
01:25:17,820 --> 01:25:19,119
Who will become the dancers?

2247
01:25:19,120 --> 01:25:21,550
Me? It can never be me.

2248
01:25:21,650 --> 01:25:22,919
I'm here for a director battle.

2249
01:25:22,920 --> 01:25:24,059
I must become the director.

2250
01:25:24,060 --> 01:25:26,490
I'm certain I will come up with something better.

2251
01:25:26,830 --> 01:25:29,129
For the production of the film draft videos,

2252
01:25:29,130 --> 01:25:31,500
you will work with the draft dancers.

2253
01:25:31,970 --> 01:25:33,769
The draft dancers...

2254
01:25:33,770 --> 01:25:37,100
will replace all ten choreographers including yourself.

2255
01:25:37,340 --> 01:25:38,609
Gosh, this is a headache.

2256
01:25:38,610 --> 01:25:41,369
Where and how will I find replacements for these people?

2257
01:25:41,370 --> 01:25:43,679
We had to cast dancers for each role.

2258
01:25:43,680 --> 01:25:46,709
They'll be the draft dancers...

2259
01:25:46,710 --> 01:25:49,519
who will be dancing in our place.

2260
01:25:49,520 --> 01:25:51,849
We need the ones who can match...

2261
01:25:51,850 --> 01:25:54,189
the lines of the choreographers...

2262
01:25:54,190 --> 01:25:55,960
along with their styles.

2263
01:25:56,060 --> 01:25:57,259
I started writing names as soon as I arrived.

2264
01:25:57,260 --> 01:25:59,459
The one who will take Koo Young's role.

2265
01:25:59,460 --> 01:26:01,459
The one who will take INGYOO's role.

2266
01:26:01,460 --> 01:26:03,759
You must prove through the video...

2267
01:26:03,760 --> 01:26:05,670
why you must become the director.

2268
01:26:05,830 --> 01:26:07,299
Just like the Class Mission, we must make the others...

2269
01:26:07,300 --> 01:26:09,380
- want to do it. - Right. That's what we have to do.

2270
01:26:09,440 --> 01:26:12,069
"Will I become the director, dancer, or choreographer?"

2271
01:26:12,070 --> 01:26:14,240
It's a mission that will determine that.

2272
01:26:14,510 --> 01:26:17,840
The title song will be revealed.

2273
01:26:17,880 --> 01:26:19,349
- What? - There's a song?

2274
01:26:19,350 --> 01:26:20,749
There's a song for this.

2275
01:26:20,750 --> 01:26:22,449
("Royalty" produced by Illmind, Yoon Mi Rae, Tiger JK)

2276
01:26:22,450 --> 01:26:24,120
- "Royalty." - "Royalty."

2277
01:26:27,620 --> 01:26:28,620
Oh!

2278
01:26:28,621 --> 01:26:30,589
It was a style that I liked.

2279
01:26:30,590 --> 01:26:32,159
"It's so good!"

2280
01:26:32,160 --> 01:26:34,329
It's so good. I think I can do a good job with it.

2281
01:26:34,330 --> 01:26:35,699
It's Yoon Mi Rae.

2282
01:26:35,700 --> 01:26:39,070
I'm someone who can work with any genre.

2283
01:26:39,170 --> 01:26:41,299
It feels like a match for me.

2284
01:26:41,300 --> 01:26:44,769
MIN JUN and Hash looked quite worried.

2285
01:26:44,770 --> 01:26:46,710
They weren't people who made drafts.

2286
01:26:47,070 --> 01:26:48,070
That's not true.

2287
01:26:48,071 --> 01:26:51,579
It was a song in a style I wanted,

2288
01:26:51,580 --> 01:26:52,580
so I felt relieved.

2289
01:26:52,581 --> 01:26:53,849
I thought I could make something nice with it.

2290
01:26:53,850 --> 01:26:55,950
I got a visual idea of what it would look like.

2291
01:26:56,350 --> 01:26:58,449
Once this mission ends,

2292
01:26:58,450 --> 01:26:59,590
for the first time,

2293
01:27:01,090 --> 01:27:03,790
two choreographers will get eliminated.

2294
01:27:03,990 --> 01:27:05,160
Oh, my gosh!

2295
01:27:05,530 --> 01:27:06,789
I got so surprised.

2296
01:27:06,790 --> 01:27:08,029
Wasn't it one person?

2297
01:27:08,030 --> 01:27:09,060
Two?

2298
01:27:09,300 --> 01:27:10,699
We're getting eliminated already?

2299
01:27:10,700 --> 01:27:12,229
Ten people did feel like a lot.

2300
01:27:12,230 --> 01:27:13,929
Eight was a better number.

2301
01:27:13,930 --> 01:27:15,370
Let's make it four.

2302
01:27:15,540 --> 01:27:16,600
Maybe five?

2303
01:27:16,700 --> 01:27:18,499
The final battle of survival...

2304
01:27:18,500 --> 01:27:20,500
that will decide the first ones to get eliminated.

2305
01:27:20,610 --> 01:27:23,240
It's the Last Stage.

2306
01:27:24,280 --> 01:27:26,350
- There are so many "lasts." - Gosh!

2307
01:27:26,450 --> 01:27:27,909
No more "lasts!"

2308
01:27:27,910 --> 01:27:31,119
Last Stage is an improvised directing battle...

2309
01:27:31,120 --> 01:27:33,189
in which the contestants must prove their worth one last time.

2310
01:27:33,190 --> 01:27:34,989
- This is going to be interesting. - This is going to be interesting.

2311
01:27:34,990 --> 01:27:38,120
The conditions of this Last Stage...

2312
01:27:38,890 --> 01:27:41,129
are 24 hours...

2313
01:27:41,130 --> 01:27:43,730
and a table and chair.

2314
01:27:44,660 --> 01:27:45,970
I feel dizzy all of a sudden.

2315
01:27:46,230 --> 01:27:48,100
That made no sense at all.

2316
01:27:48,400 --> 01:27:50,720
It stressed me out. It was going to make my hair fall out.

2317
01:27:50,770 --> 01:27:52,669
Within 24 hours,

2318
01:27:52,670 --> 01:27:54,839
you must create your own work...

2319
01:27:54,840 --> 01:27:57,080
including the table and chair.

2320
01:27:57,210 --> 01:27:58,650
I'm about to go crazy.

2321
01:27:58,910 --> 01:28:00,050
(Sighing)

2322
01:28:00,250 --> 01:28:01,409
On top of that,

2323
01:28:01,410 --> 01:28:03,319
the one who becomes the director of this mission...

2324
01:28:03,320 --> 01:28:05,350
will be exempted from elimination.

2325
01:28:07,750 --> 01:28:09,459
The director will also be given...

2326
01:28:09,460 --> 01:28:11,540
the right to decide on the elimination candidates...

2327
01:28:11,620 --> 01:28:13,629
as a Judge.

2328
01:28:13,630 --> 01:28:15,259
Gosh! I didn't expect that at all.

2329
01:28:15,260 --> 01:28:17,259
I must win that position.

2330
01:28:17,260 --> 01:28:18,559
Really? Gosh.

2331
01:28:18,560 --> 01:28:19,699
The director becomes the Judge.

2332
01:28:19,700 --> 01:28:21,529
That was an unbelievable benefit.

2333
01:28:21,530 --> 01:28:22,969
I got so surprised. The director becomes the Judge.

2334
01:28:22,970 --> 01:28:24,140
It felt so cruel.

2335
01:28:24,370 --> 01:28:25,709
After becoming the director,

2336
01:28:25,710 --> 01:28:28,540
being able to enter the safe zone is a big benefit in itself.

2337
01:28:28,740 --> 01:28:30,940
They did well to make everyone want that position.

2338
01:28:31,240 --> 01:28:33,210
It's an actual war.

2339
01:28:33,510 --> 01:28:35,550
I will make sure to put up my name as the director.

2340
01:28:35,850 --> 01:28:39,649
Thus, beyond securing survival,

2341
01:28:39,650 --> 01:28:42,459
the director will be in a position to be able to...

2342
01:28:42,460 --> 01:28:44,096
decide on the fates of the other choreographers.

2343
01:28:44,120 --> 01:28:46,529
One of us will take the throne...

2344
01:28:46,530 --> 01:28:49,160
and handle the others like slaves.

2345
01:28:49,360 --> 01:28:51,499
The Title Sequence Film Mission...

2346
01:28:51,500 --> 01:28:54,929
isn't just about coming up with the title of the show.

2347
01:28:54,930 --> 01:28:57,439
Only one director will be chosen...

2348
01:28:57,440 --> 01:28:59,839
and the elimination candidates who will head to the Last Stage...

2349
01:28:59,840 --> 01:29:02,610
will be decided through this mission.

2350
01:29:02,640 --> 01:29:04,039
That's a huge right.

2351
01:29:04,040 --> 01:29:05,879
It's a position that everyone would want.

2352
01:29:05,880 --> 01:29:07,849
I believe the director can choose...

2353
01:29:07,850 --> 01:29:09,050
who to eliminate.

2354
01:29:09,250 --> 01:29:10,250
I must win.

2355
01:29:10,251 --> 01:29:11,849
It's because I must become the champion.

2356
01:29:11,850 --> 01:29:13,119
That can never happen.

2357
01:29:13,120 --> 01:29:14,950
I will survive until the end.

2358
01:29:15,760 --> 01:29:16,959
In Directors' War,

2359
01:29:16,960 --> 01:29:18,660
isn't that the biggest authority?

2360
01:29:19,490 --> 01:29:20,759
Right away?

2361
01:29:20,760 --> 01:29:22,500
This is a casting war.

2362
01:29:22,700 --> 01:29:24,759
Finding dancers is the problem.

2363
01:29:24,760 --> 01:29:26,929
I must get to them first before the others.

2364
01:29:26,930 --> 01:29:27,999
Should I call them now?

2365
01:29:28,000 --> 01:29:29,999
I must call the dancers.

2366
01:29:30,000 --> 01:29:33,110
I have to find dancers who can take our roles.

2367
01:29:33,510 --> 01:29:34,840
Isn't this insane?

2368
01:29:34,970 --> 01:29:35,979
I'm going to lose my hair.

2369
01:29:35,980 --> 01:29:38,410
Are you going to get me a hair transplant?

2370
01:29:38,850 --> 01:29:41,649
The dancers have to suit all ten of our characters.

2371
01:29:41,650 --> 01:29:43,849
I must make the choreographers want to perform my work.

2372
01:29:43,850 --> 01:29:47,049
I must film a draft that can bring out...

2373
01:29:47,050 --> 01:29:48,589
each choreographer's qualities...

2374
01:29:48,590 --> 01:29:50,559
to be able to get a lot of votes and become the director.

2375
01:29:50,560 --> 01:29:52,690
It's hard to find the dancers.

2376
01:29:53,030 --> 01:29:58,160
Gosh, I think Tae Woo will call Nino.

2377
01:29:59,030 --> 01:30:00,030
(Peeking at Kasper's room)

2378
01:30:00,031 --> 01:30:02,570
Who should I call?

2379
01:30:02,740 --> 01:30:06,370
I had to call the dancers I wanted first.

2380
01:30:06,570 --> 01:30:08,269
Nino will take INGYOO's role.

2381
01:30:08,270 --> 01:30:10,639
Nino has a sense of arrogance to him.

2382
01:30:10,640 --> 01:30:12,649
I thought he was a perfect match as a character.

2383
01:30:12,650 --> 01:30:15,750
I thought Nino was suitable for that role.

2384
01:30:16,150 --> 01:30:17,949
If he doesn't work with me,

2385
01:30:17,950 --> 01:30:19,220
it's pure betrayal.

2386
01:30:19,350 --> 01:30:20,990
Shuri will take BADA's role.

2387
01:30:21,520 --> 01:30:22,689
(He calls Shuri right away.)

2388
01:30:22,690 --> 01:30:24,089
Hey, Shuri.

2389
01:30:24,090 --> 01:30:25,660
I called to cast you.

2390
01:30:25,790 --> 01:30:27,060
Shuri for Kasper's role.

2391
01:30:27,330 --> 01:30:28,330
Shuri!

2392
01:30:28,331 --> 01:30:30,399
Shuri will definitely ask Kasper.

2393
01:30:30,400 --> 01:30:32,000
(Kasper's role: Shuri)

2394
01:30:32,230 --> 01:30:34,570
Shuri for Kasper's role.

2395
01:30:34,770 --> 01:30:36,569
I think everyone will think the same.

2396
01:30:36,570 --> 01:30:38,169
I must move quickly.

2397
01:30:38,170 --> 01:30:41,309
The only one who can cover his skills and damping...

2398
01:30:41,310 --> 01:30:42,879
is Shuri in my opinion.

2399
01:30:42,880 --> 01:30:44,309
I contacted Shuri.

2400
01:30:44,310 --> 01:30:45,549
(Shuri! Can you join me for a draft mission on June 2?)

2401
01:30:45,550 --> 01:30:47,450
I didn't get back from him yet.

2402
01:30:48,210 --> 01:30:49,919
Why are you all gathered together?

2403
01:30:49,920 --> 01:30:52,520
Koo Young's role is the hardest.

2404
01:30:52,650 --> 01:30:54,650
Koo Young's role is the hardest.

2405
01:30:56,190 --> 01:30:57,320
(Peeking)

2406
01:30:58,090 --> 01:30:59,229
(Peeking)

2407
01:30:59,230 --> 01:31:01,559
(Gazing)

2408
01:31:01,560 --> 01:31:03,329
You look busy. Who contacted you?

2409
01:31:03,330 --> 01:31:04,330
No.

2410
01:31:04,730 --> 01:31:06,130
Shuri contacted me.

2411
01:31:06,400 --> 01:31:07,869
What?

2412
01:31:07,870 --> 01:31:09,340
No way.

2413
01:31:09,400 --> 01:31:11,600
He told me that BADA contacted him.

2414
01:31:11,770 --> 01:31:13,639
(Screaming)

2415
01:31:13,640 --> 01:31:16,480
(Escaping reality)

2416
01:31:16,910 --> 01:31:18,740
That got me flustered quite a lot.

2417
01:31:18,910 --> 01:31:21,749
This punk read my message and didn't reply.

2418
01:31:21,750 --> 01:31:23,619
That was why I texted him again.

2419
01:31:23,620 --> 01:31:25,719
"Why aren't you answering me? Please join me."

2420
01:31:25,720 --> 01:31:28,089
Shuri will come to me this time.

2421
01:31:28,090 --> 01:31:29,360
He is only human.

2422
01:31:29,460 --> 01:31:32,560
(Shuri was cast by 4 choreographers.)

2423
01:31:32,660 --> 01:31:34,930
This is a battle for Shuri.

2424
01:31:35,600 --> 01:31:37,829
Shuri is my child.

2425
01:31:37,830 --> 01:31:39,399
I can never get him taken away from me.

2426
01:31:39,400 --> 01:31:42,029
Without thinking about the consequences,

2427
01:31:42,030 --> 01:31:43,999
I'm going to go for the best way possible.

2428
01:31:44,000 --> 01:31:45,809
I'm confident when it comes to films.

2429
01:31:45,810 --> 01:31:47,439
I'm 100 percent certain about this.

2430
01:31:47,440 --> 01:31:49,139
The others are here to prove themselves.

2431
01:31:49,140 --> 01:31:51,510
I must be able to prove myself as well.

2432
01:31:51,840 --> 01:31:54,250
The title of director is mine.

2433
01:31:57,150 --> 01:31:59,150
(D-Day of Title Sequence Film Mission draft shoot)

2434
01:32:01,450 --> 01:32:02,619
Thank you.

2435
01:32:02,620 --> 01:32:05,290
(The 10 directors and dancers have gathered for the draft shoot.)

2436
01:32:06,160 --> 01:32:09,399
Thank you so much for helping out with the draft.

2437
01:32:09,400 --> 01:32:11,899
Each of you will become the director...

2438
01:32:11,900 --> 01:32:13,800
for this draft.

2439
01:32:13,930 --> 01:32:15,329
Many of our dancers have gathered...

2440
01:32:15,330 --> 01:32:17,069
to help me out.

2441
01:32:17,070 --> 01:32:20,269
The dancers are really important during the draft shoot.

2442
01:32:20,270 --> 01:32:21,969
I felt this while being a director.

2443
01:32:21,970 --> 01:32:24,139
Choreographies get chosen...

2444
01:32:24,140 --> 01:32:27,009
based on the draft dancers.

2445
01:32:27,010 --> 01:32:28,949
That's how important they are.

2446
01:32:28,950 --> 01:32:31,350
But I hit a red light based on that.

2447
01:32:32,220 --> 01:32:34,490
BADA! Shuri will take BADA's role.

2448
01:32:35,720 --> 01:32:37,159
(Team Kasper: BADA's role, Shuri)

2449
01:32:37,160 --> 01:32:38,759
He's like a son to me.

2450
01:32:38,760 --> 01:32:40,730
He's always assisting me.

2451
01:32:40,860 --> 01:32:42,560
Kasper!

2452
01:32:44,560 --> 01:32:46,670
(She didn't get a reply from him yesterday.)

2453
01:32:46,900 --> 01:32:48,099
Shuri!

2454
01:32:48,100 --> 01:32:49,639
(Team BADA: Kasper's role, Shuri)

2455
01:32:49,640 --> 01:32:51,970
You're the only one who can take this role.

2456
01:32:52,440 --> 01:32:53,939
But with Shuri...

2457
01:32:53,940 --> 01:32:55,709
That's impossible.

2458
01:32:55,710 --> 01:32:56,879
Even if he wants to help out with all of us,

2459
01:32:56,880 --> 01:32:59,049
it's right for us to avoid using him.

2460
01:32:59,050 --> 01:33:00,690
I'll step away from the battle for Shuri.

2461
01:33:01,050 --> 01:33:03,420
Hoi will take Kasper's role.

2462
01:33:04,320 --> 01:33:06,650
(In sync with Kasper 100 percent?)

2463
01:33:06,820 --> 01:33:08,150
And Kasper.

2464
01:33:08,650 --> 01:33:10,389
Kasper is my key ring guy.

2465
01:33:10,390 --> 01:33:12,389
He will become the key ring guy of the key ring guy.

2466
01:33:12,390 --> 01:33:13,559
He's working hard.

2467
01:33:13,560 --> 01:33:15,589
And INGYOO's role...

2468
01:33:15,590 --> 01:33:17,229
(Team BABYZOO: INGYOO's role)

2469
01:33:17,230 --> 01:33:19,269
will be taken by Lee Jung!

2470
01:33:19,270 --> 01:33:21,470
(Fully acceptable)

2471
01:33:21,530 --> 01:33:22,599
It's because...

2472
01:33:22,600 --> 01:33:23,940
(INJUNG's "like JENNIE")

2473
01:33:24,140 --> 01:33:28,639
Lee Jung has been friends with INGYOO for a decade.

2474
01:33:28,640 --> 01:33:29,640
Yes, right.

2475
01:33:29,641 --> 01:33:32,309
She understands INGYOO's characteristics so well.

2476
01:33:32,310 --> 01:33:34,309
- Exactly! - Right.

2477
01:33:34,310 --> 01:33:35,310
INGYOO.

2478
01:33:35,311 --> 01:33:36,949
(Team Back Koo Young: INGYOO's role, no: ze)

2479
01:33:36,950 --> 01:33:37,950
Okay!

2480
01:33:37,951 --> 01:33:39,449
You've grown much taller, INGYOO.

2481
01:33:39,450 --> 01:33:40,450
(Laughing)

2482
01:33:40,451 --> 01:33:42,759
She's incredible with these drafts.

2483
01:33:42,760 --> 01:33:45,590
And here's Ms. Lia Kim.

2484
01:33:45,760 --> 01:33:47,229
- Hash! - Right.

2485
01:33:47,230 --> 01:33:49,059
- I did my hair just like hers. - Right.

2486
01:33:49,060 --> 01:33:50,729
- The side-swept bangs. - Right.

2487
01:33:50,730 --> 01:33:52,729
Hash is really flexible.

2488
01:33:52,730 --> 01:33:54,429
She can pull off all kinds of techniques.

2489
01:33:54,430 --> 01:33:55,900
Right! These moves!

2490
01:33:56,470 --> 01:33:57,640
- These moves! - "I got it!"

2491
01:33:57,900 --> 01:33:59,339
We must dance like the ones we're given?

2492
01:33:59,340 --> 01:34:01,169
- Well... - While imagining that person?

2493
01:34:01,170 --> 01:34:02,739
Don't dance like them.

2494
01:34:02,740 --> 01:34:05,539
Say this to BADA, "You want to do this, don't you?"

2495
01:34:05,540 --> 01:34:07,109
This is a better approach.

2496
01:34:07,110 --> 01:34:09,449
It's like, "You want to do this, don't you, Koo Young?"

2497
01:34:09,450 --> 01:34:10,649
(Vata is confused.)

2498
01:34:10,650 --> 01:34:14,419
It's the draft of the Title Sequence Film Mission.

2499
01:34:14,420 --> 01:34:18,619
What's being seen now is a completely rough draft.

2500
01:34:18,620 --> 01:34:21,060
I'm quite detailed when filming for drafts.

2501
01:34:21,660 --> 01:34:23,829
Are the lights different in color on purpose?

2502
01:34:23,830 --> 01:34:25,529
- We're working on them. - Okay.

2503
01:34:25,530 --> 01:34:27,029
This is the only mood light.

2504
01:34:27,030 --> 01:34:28,369
Is this the spotlight?

2505
01:34:28,370 --> 01:34:30,140
- It's the spotlight. - Okay.

2506
01:34:30,470 --> 01:34:33,140
As soon as the spotlight turned on, the blue light disappears.

2507
01:34:33,640 --> 01:34:34,710
This one.

2508
01:34:34,970 --> 01:34:36,579
I think this is the right tone for the blue one.

2509
01:34:36,580 --> 01:34:38,979
The key point of the Title Sequence.

2510
01:34:38,980 --> 01:34:40,149
The lights.

2511
01:34:40,150 --> 01:34:42,549
There's a certain mood that can be felt from the lights.

2512
01:34:42,550 --> 01:34:44,019
Something only the lights can express.

2513
01:34:44,020 --> 01:34:45,619
Only the lights are expressed in the video...

2514
01:34:45,620 --> 01:34:47,819
and only the lights can lighten up the stage.

2515
01:34:47,820 --> 01:34:49,559
The dancers under those lights.

2516
01:34:49,560 --> 01:34:51,360
"How will the mood feel with the lights?"

2517
01:34:51,590 --> 01:34:53,560
The lights control the mood.

2518
01:34:54,190 --> 01:34:55,960
- Hey. - Yes?

2519
01:34:56,060 --> 01:34:57,830
Come here, Ye Hwan.

2520
01:34:58,060 --> 01:35:00,300
Ye Hwan has Koo Young's role.

2521
01:35:00,400 --> 01:35:03,370
You will be given a very important mission.

2522
01:35:03,570 --> 01:35:05,070
You're part of the lighting crew now.

2523
01:35:06,210 --> 01:35:09,180
Here. Like this.

2524
01:35:09,640 --> 01:35:10,680
This is really important.

2525
01:35:10,980 --> 01:35:12,079
At this pace?

2526
01:35:12,080 --> 01:35:15,920
Right. Boom!

2527
01:35:16,150 --> 01:35:18,220
The cameraman will come.

2528
01:35:18,720 --> 01:35:19,850
At that moment...

2529
01:35:19,950 --> 01:35:23,559
Flash!

2530
01:35:23,560 --> 01:35:25,040
Flash the light constantly like this.

2531
01:35:25,490 --> 01:35:26,490
Okay!

2532
01:35:26,990 --> 01:35:28,630
(Take 1, 1st attempt)

2533
01:35:28,730 --> 01:35:29,959
Nice!

2534
01:35:29,960 --> 01:35:32,929
(In the zone)

2535
01:35:32,930 --> 01:35:34,369
You shouldn't shine it downward, Ye Hwan.

2536
01:35:34,370 --> 01:35:36,070
The light has to lighten up everything.

2537
01:35:37,040 --> 01:35:39,340
(Take 2, lighting the whole room)

2538
01:35:39,440 --> 01:35:41,139
Don't feel the rhythm too much.

2539
01:35:41,140 --> 01:35:43,710
Move it around gently.

2540
01:35:43,880 --> 01:35:46,649
(Take 3, moving slowly)

2541
01:35:46,650 --> 01:35:48,349
You have to move from here to here.

2542
01:35:48,350 --> 01:35:50,119
(Lighting it slowly toward the front)

2543
01:35:50,120 --> 01:35:51,319
(The cameraman is satisfied.)

2544
01:35:51,320 --> 01:35:52,550
We did it!

2545
01:35:53,320 --> 01:35:54,666
(The key ring guy of the light lover is found.)

2546
01:35:54,690 --> 01:35:57,860
The biggest focus is on me becoming the director.

2547
01:35:58,220 --> 01:35:59,230
I must get that title.

2548
01:35:59,390 --> 01:36:02,260
It's a problem if I lose to them, isn't it?

2549
01:36:02,530 --> 01:36:04,500
A punk like Kasper... No.

2550
01:36:05,130 --> 01:36:06,230
Gosh!

2551
01:36:06,930 --> 01:36:09,369
Guys like them will give me directions.

2552
01:36:09,370 --> 01:36:12,140
"Hey, move back more to the left!"

2553
01:36:12,240 --> 01:36:14,309
That is what will happen to me.

2554
01:36:14,310 --> 01:36:16,270
If that happens, I must head back to my hometown.

2555
01:36:17,440 --> 01:36:18,480
Yes!

2556
01:36:18,910 --> 01:36:20,709
During the Signature 400 Mission,

2557
01:36:20,710 --> 01:36:22,670
I wasn't able to get my name on the Credit Board.

2558
01:36:25,920 --> 01:36:28,420
With this mission,

2559
01:36:28,520 --> 01:36:31,259
the director's name will appear during every episode.

2560
01:36:31,260 --> 01:36:32,630
I must show everyone who I am.

2561
01:36:32,790 --> 01:36:34,130
I want to become the director.

2562
01:36:34,260 --> 01:36:35,900
Please help me become the director!

2563
01:36:36,600 --> 01:36:38,760
I'm satisfied with the draft.

2564
01:36:38,860 --> 01:36:42,099
The one-minute video that will represent this show.

2565
01:36:42,100 --> 01:36:43,100
I felt confident.

2566
01:36:43,470 --> 01:36:46,210
Great! I love this place.

2567
01:36:47,170 --> 01:36:48,239
Let's go!

2568
01:36:48,240 --> 01:36:49,279
(Showroom)

2569
01:36:49,280 --> 01:36:50,739
(The place responsible for the casual looks of the directors)

2570
01:36:50,740 --> 01:36:52,779
Should we enter the showroom?

2571
01:36:52,780 --> 01:36:54,449
- Yes! - Yes!

2572
01:36:54,450 --> 01:36:55,649
We're wearing their pants.

2573
01:36:55,650 --> 01:36:57,150
Right. The pants.

2574
01:36:57,350 --> 01:36:58,919
Black and gray!

2575
01:36:58,920 --> 01:36:59,920
(Today's OOTD: Black and gray)

2576
01:36:59,921 --> 01:37:01,449
I really wanted those.

2577
01:37:01,450 --> 01:37:03,289
- The black ones? - The black ones look nice.

2578
01:37:03,290 --> 01:37:04,760
It's such a nice fit.

2579
01:37:05,460 --> 01:37:07,560
I really wanted this.

2580
01:37:07,660 --> 01:37:09,460
The color that suits cool tones.

2581
01:37:09,560 --> 01:37:10,799
- Yes! - Nice!

2582
01:37:10,800 --> 01:37:12,200
- How's the color? - It looks nice.

2583
01:37:13,470 --> 01:37:16,040
It looks nice, doesn't it? I want it!

2584
01:37:16,140 --> 01:37:18,300
(BABYZOO's pick is the stylish gray windbreaker.)

2585
01:37:18,570 --> 01:37:20,010
Are the colors the same, NaiN?

2586
01:37:20,110 --> 01:37:22,780
Your setup is insane right now.

2587
01:37:23,410 --> 01:37:24,610
This really looks nice.

2588
01:37:24,840 --> 01:37:26,749
It looks really nice when I wear it.

2589
01:37:26,750 --> 01:37:28,609
"It looks really nice when I wear it."

2590
01:37:28,610 --> 01:37:30,170
- Gosh! - What kind of comment is that?

2591
01:37:31,720 --> 01:37:34,289
A vivid color like this suits MIN JUN.

2592
01:37:34,290 --> 01:37:35,319
Right.

2593
01:37:35,320 --> 01:37:36,996
(He gets excited after hearing his compliment.)

2594
01:37:37,020 --> 01:37:38,720
(I feel great.)

2595
01:37:39,020 --> 01:37:40,829
- Gray! - Gray!

2596
01:37:40,830 --> 01:37:41,830
(They get ready to work...)

2597
01:37:41,831 --> 01:37:42,976
(after brightening up their moods with some shopping.)

2598
01:37:43,000 --> 01:37:44,300
Let's see how everyone does.

2599
01:37:44,800 --> 01:37:48,199
I'm expecting great qualities from everyone.

2600
01:37:48,200 --> 01:37:49,320
It's making me feel nervous.

2601
01:37:49,670 --> 01:37:52,570
Gosh! I feel quite satisfied.

2602
01:37:52,670 --> 01:37:54,409
After putting together the video yesterday,

2603
01:37:54,410 --> 01:37:56,910
I thought that I should be the one to become director.

2604
01:37:57,610 --> 01:37:58,980
Oh, gosh!

2605
01:37:59,810 --> 01:38:00,909
(A video is played in all rooms of the directors.)

2606
01:38:00,910 --> 01:38:01,950
(What's this?)

2607
01:38:02,720 --> 01:38:05,319
I will now explain how the director will get chosen...

2608
01:38:05,320 --> 01:38:07,590
for the Title Sequence Film Mission.

2609
01:38:07,850 --> 01:38:09,560
How the director will get chosen.

2610
01:38:09,960 --> 01:38:11,120
I was curious about this.

2611
01:38:11,220 --> 01:38:12,289
Hold on! We have to watch this together.

2612
01:38:12,290 --> 01:38:13,610
Why am I watching this on my own.

2613
01:38:13,660 --> 01:38:16,259
The ten choreographers will first reveal...

2614
01:38:16,260 --> 01:38:19,060
the film draft videos they worked on.

2615
01:38:19,160 --> 01:38:20,700
Before revealing the video,

2616
01:38:20,800 --> 01:38:23,369
each choreographer must explain the key points...

2617
01:38:23,370 --> 01:38:26,239
of the visuals, story, and characters.

2618
01:38:26,240 --> 01:38:28,639
The directions of the video must be explained.

2619
01:38:28,640 --> 01:38:30,680
Gosh, we have to make a presentation?

2620
01:38:30,780 --> 01:38:33,010
Once the film draft videos get revealed,

2621
01:38:33,110 --> 01:38:35,550
through an evaluation of the choreographers...

2622
01:38:35,650 --> 01:38:38,319
two director candidates will get decided.

2623
01:38:38,320 --> 01:38:42,450
The 2 director candidates will use 9 dancers...

2624
01:38:42,550 --> 01:38:45,260
to complete the final draft video.

2625
01:38:45,420 --> 01:38:47,189
The director candidates...

2626
01:38:47,190 --> 01:38:49,660
will participate in each other's videos.

2627
01:38:49,860 --> 01:38:50,860
(What?)

2628
01:38:50,860 --> 01:38:51,860
(Freezing)

2629
01:38:51,861 --> 01:38:53,269
So we should do it twice?

2630
01:38:53,270 --> 01:38:54,769
The draft videos...

2631
01:38:54,770 --> 01:38:56,169
must be performed by the actual choreographers...

2632
01:38:56,170 --> 01:38:58,470
under two directors?

2633
01:38:58,570 --> 01:39:01,309
It's going to be so hard if I don't become the director.

2634
01:39:01,310 --> 01:39:04,040
Sharing things is inevitable in this situation.

2635
01:39:04,580 --> 01:39:07,349
It's a matter of who doesn't get shaken and maintains their style.

2636
01:39:07,350 --> 01:39:09,650
Is there another way to decide...

2637
01:39:10,120 --> 01:39:11,480
the final director out of the two?

2638
01:39:11,520 --> 01:39:14,319
The final director of the Title Sequence Film Mission...

2639
01:39:14,320 --> 01:39:16,089
will be decided by the final draft videos...

2640
01:39:16,090 --> 01:39:18,459
made by the two director candidates.

2641
01:39:18,460 --> 01:39:19,989
The votes of eight choreographers...

2642
01:39:19,990 --> 01:39:21,930
excluding the two director candidates...

2643
01:39:22,190 --> 01:39:25,060
and one vote of the Public Judge will decide the final director.

2644
01:39:25,160 --> 01:39:27,030
The other eight choreographers...

2645
01:39:27,130 --> 01:39:31,100
will evaluate the directing skills...

2646
01:39:31,200 --> 01:39:32,769
of the two director candidates.

2647
01:39:32,770 --> 01:39:34,109
I must become a candidate.

2648
01:39:34,110 --> 01:39:35,810
Pick me!

2649
01:39:35,940 --> 01:39:38,040
I hope I become one of the two candidates.

2650
01:39:38,140 --> 01:39:41,910
As a result, the one candidate with the most votes...

2651
01:39:42,010 --> 01:39:44,119
will become the director of the Title Sequence Film...

2652
01:39:44,120 --> 01:39:47,150
of Street World Fighter: Directors' War.

2653
01:39:47,320 --> 01:39:49,189
The final director...

2654
01:39:49,190 --> 01:39:52,560
will also be given the right of the Judge...

2655
01:39:53,030 --> 01:39:55,130
to decide on the candidates for the Last Stage.

2656
01:39:55,430 --> 01:39:56,999
(Screaming)

2657
01:39:57,000 --> 01:39:58,730
That's so scary!

2658
01:39:58,830 --> 01:40:01,899
I really hope it isn't me.

2659
01:40:01,900 --> 01:40:04,699
Gosh, that's quite scary. I don't like that.

2660
01:40:04,700 --> 01:40:07,369
I will be in danger if I don't become the director.

2661
01:40:07,370 --> 01:40:08,569
That made me feel scared.

2662
01:40:08,570 --> 01:40:10,239
Even after become a director candidate,

2663
01:40:10,240 --> 01:40:11,909
that person can also end up being on the Last Stage...

2664
01:40:11,910 --> 01:40:14,650
if they fail to become the final director.

2665
01:40:16,250 --> 01:40:19,150
Gosh! Someone will feel a lot of stress.

2666
01:40:19,320 --> 01:40:21,120
Out of the ten choreographers,

2667
01:40:21,220 --> 01:40:23,359
who will become the director...

2668
01:40:23,360 --> 01:40:24,759
to complete the first scene...

2669
01:40:24,760 --> 01:40:27,230
of Street World Fighter: Directors' War?

2670
01:40:27,530 --> 01:40:30,030
Me! I hope it's me.

2671
01:40:30,360 --> 01:40:31,500
It will definitely be me...

2672
01:40:32,560 --> 01:40:35,200
and Back Koo Young.

2673
01:40:35,370 --> 01:40:39,839
Even after hearing that there were going to be two director candidates,

2674
01:40:39,840 --> 01:40:40,840
I felt confident.

2675
01:40:40,841 --> 01:40:43,140
It won't make sense if mine doesn't get picked.

2676
01:40:43,440 --> 01:40:44,580
I'm really confident.

2677
01:40:44,880 --> 01:40:47,109
I put together a video...

2678
01:40:47,110 --> 01:40:50,019
that will make the others want to perform it.

2679
01:40:50,020 --> 01:40:51,020
I'm confident.

2680
01:40:51,650 --> 01:40:53,690
(Concept and film draft video reveal)

2681
01:40:53,850 --> 01:40:55,149
(The concept and video reveal begins.)

2682
01:40:55,150 --> 01:40:57,420
Oh, no!

2683
01:40:58,220 --> 01:40:59,290
I'm scared!

2684
01:40:59,590 --> 01:41:00,889
(Concept and film draft video reveal)

2685
01:41:00,890 --> 01:41:04,960
Hello. I'm the first one up. I'm BABYZOO.

2686
01:41:05,330 --> 01:41:07,000
(Excited)

2687
01:41:07,070 --> 01:41:08,130
I'm so curious.

2688
01:41:08,600 --> 01:41:10,300
BABYZOO worked really hard.

2689
01:41:10,400 --> 01:41:12,569
The Title Sequence Film...

2690
01:41:12,570 --> 01:41:16,139
is the first video that gets revealed to the public.

2691
01:41:16,140 --> 01:41:20,350
The one-minute video that will represent this show.

2692
01:41:20,550 --> 01:41:22,550
The ones who watch the show...

2693
01:41:22,650 --> 01:41:23,820
are the viewers.

2694
01:41:23,920 --> 01:41:25,850
Mass appeal can't be ignored.

2695
01:41:26,020 --> 01:41:27,590
As it's that kind of video,

2696
01:41:27,790 --> 01:41:30,460
I slightly made a light approach.

2697
01:41:30,690 --> 01:41:33,389
You will notice when you watch the draft video.

2698
01:41:33,390 --> 01:41:36,399
The intro had "Countdown."

2699
01:41:36,400 --> 01:41:37,530
"Countdown?"

2700
01:41:37,630 --> 01:41:42,129
I worked on a pose before the start of a race.

2701
01:41:42,130 --> 01:41:44,439
The stopwatch is pressed to announce our start.

2702
01:41:44,440 --> 01:41:48,169
We did hand signs with each other to represent a good competition.

2703
01:41:48,170 --> 01:41:50,879
There are 5 men and 5 women.

2704
01:41:50,880 --> 01:41:52,680
I thought a pair move was necessary.

2705
01:41:54,750 --> 01:41:57,920
(The pair part is quite hot.)

2706
01:41:58,320 --> 01:42:02,020
I believed the public would like that part.

2707
01:42:02,550 --> 01:42:04,760
Then, what exactly is the concept?

2708
01:42:04,860 --> 01:42:06,730
Is it a race or...

2709
01:42:06,830 --> 01:42:08,359
I think the concept...

2710
01:42:08,360 --> 01:42:10,660
is that we're starting a competition together.

2711
01:42:10,760 --> 01:42:13,230
There wasn't a specific concept.

2712
01:42:13,330 --> 01:42:16,300
It was a piece that was focused toward the public.

2713
01:42:16,470 --> 01:42:18,099
I think the public...

2714
01:42:18,100 --> 01:42:19,569
The public will be...

2715
01:42:19,570 --> 01:42:21,539
The public...

2716
01:42:21,540 --> 01:42:24,410
It exceeds the quality I expected.

2717
01:42:24,640 --> 01:42:26,580
I'm sure the public will love it.

2718
01:42:26,750 --> 01:42:27,750
I'm confident.

2719
01:42:27,950 --> 01:42:29,620
- Are we watching it now? - I'm excited.

2720
01:42:29,750 --> 01:42:31,220
I'm excited!

2721
01:42:31,550 --> 01:42:32,849
(Title Sequence Film Mission)

2722
01:42:32,850 --> 01:42:34,610
(Choreography Concept Credit Board, BABYZOO)

2723
01:42:36,050 --> 01:42:37,260
I like the "Countdown" part.

2724
01:42:43,200 --> 01:42:44,360
It's Renan!

2725
01:42:45,930 --> 01:42:47,570
Lee Jung took INGYOO's role?

2726
01:42:54,170 --> 01:42:55,510
Why do I look so excited?

2727
01:42:58,140 --> 01:42:59,140
It's fancy.

2728
01:42:59,380 --> 01:43:00,750
Gosh, that's amazing.

2729
01:43:01,750 --> 01:43:02,950
That's impressive!

2730
01:43:03,450 --> 01:43:05,650
Yes! Kasper!

2731
01:43:07,120 --> 01:43:08,190
Hey!

2732
01:43:09,020 --> 01:43:10,060
It's really nice.

2733
01:43:12,020 --> 01:43:13,330
Hyun Se is playing my role?

2734
01:43:13,430 --> 01:43:15,260
This part suits BADA.

2735
01:43:19,460 --> 01:43:21,330
It's dancing from start to finish.

2736
01:43:22,670 --> 01:43:23,800
They're dancing in pairs!

2737
01:43:31,610 --> 01:43:32,839
This looks nice.

2738
01:43:32,840 --> 01:43:33,850
I also like this part.

2739
01:43:37,420 --> 01:43:39,549
(You can watch BABYZOO's full video on "The CHOOM" and "Mnet Plus.")

2740
01:43:39,550 --> 01:43:40,789
- Nice! - Nice!

2741
01:43:40,790 --> 01:43:41,890
That was exciting.

2742
01:43:41,990 --> 01:43:42,990
This move looks cool.

2743
01:43:43,290 --> 01:43:44,419
I would've never thought of that.

2744
01:43:44,420 --> 01:43:45,760
(I'll bite my top as well.)

2745
01:43:45,960 --> 01:43:48,830
Gosh, that was nice. He did well with the choreography.

2746
01:43:48,990 --> 01:43:50,559
I loved the biting part.

2747
01:43:50,560 --> 01:43:52,459
The flow of the choreography was really nice.

2748
01:43:52,460 --> 01:43:55,429
It looked so exciting that I wanted to learn it.

2749
01:43:55,430 --> 01:43:58,440
Many people said the choreography was nice.

2750
01:43:58,940 --> 01:44:00,539
(Chuckling)

2751
01:44:00,540 --> 01:44:01,540
Yes!

2752
01:44:01,541 --> 01:44:03,210
To be honest, it felt great.

2753
01:44:03,510 --> 01:44:04,940
It was really nice.

2754
01:44:05,310 --> 01:44:09,050
But one thing that was disappointing...

2755
01:44:09,450 --> 01:44:10,450
What?

2756
01:44:10,720 --> 01:44:12,520
Was the pair part.

2757
01:44:14,420 --> 01:44:15,796
(The pair part of 5 men and 5 women)

2758
01:44:15,820 --> 01:44:18,319
It was a good idea as there were men and women.

2759
01:44:18,320 --> 01:44:19,929
But this is what gets me.

2760
01:44:19,930 --> 01:44:21,790
"We have to watch pair parts every episode?"

2761
01:44:21,860 --> 01:44:24,859
The theme of theTitle Sequence Film Mission...

2762
01:44:24,860 --> 01:44:27,400
was to represent our show and the ten choreographers.

2763
01:44:27,500 --> 01:44:28,899
A pair part all of a sudden?

2764
01:44:28,900 --> 01:44:30,700
Twerking was done out of nowhere.

2765
01:44:31,470 --> 01:44:32,470
There are many pair moves out there,

2766
01:44:32,471 --> 01:44:33,769
but in afro dancing,

2767
01:44:33,770 --> 01:44:36,170
there should be something sensual.

2768
01:44:39,380 --> 01:44:41,850
It was funny to see MIN JUN and Hash as a pair.

2769
01:44:44,220 --> 01:44:45,519
In the video, MIN JUN gestured pulling...

2770
01:44:45,520 --> 01:44:47,349
Hash's hips up and down.

2771
01:44:47,350 --> 01:44:48,450
I found that funny.

2772
01:44:50,560 --> 01:44:52,059
(MIN JUN, Hash)

2773
01:44:52,060 --> 01:44:54,136
In the choreography, I had to bounce my hips up and down.

2774
01:44:54,160 --> 01:44:55,429
Then MIN JUN had to pretend to pull.

2775
01:44:55,430 --> 01:44:57,160
That was quite shocking.

2776
01:44:57,300 --> 01:44:59,420
I found it funny that I had to do the same with NaiN.

2777
01:45:00,130 --> 01:45:01,629
(INGYOO and NaiN are twerking side by side.)

2778
01:45:01,630 --> 01:45:03,510
So watching your choreography made me wonder...

2779
01:45:04,040 --> 01:45:06,709
if the direction matched...

2780
01:45:06,710 --> 01:45:08,710
the level of directors here.

2781
01:45:08,810 --> 01:45:11,880
(Surprised by his blunt comment)

2782
01:45:11,940 --> 01:45:13,250
I just didn't get it.

2783
01:45:13,280 --> 01:45:14,349
Why were...

2784
01:45:14,350 --> 01:45:16,420
female directors suddenly twerking?

2785
01:45:16,520 --> 01:45:18,419
He failed to capture the gravitas...

2786
01:45:18,420 --> 01:45:19,719
of the directors.

2787
01:45:19,720 --> 01:45:20,720
The pair dance?

2788
01:45:20,721 --> 01:45:22,249
I'm certain of this.

2789
01:45:22,250 --> 01:45:24,219
If the viewers watch my video,

2790
01:45:24,220 --> 01:45:26,729
they'll go, "I'd love to see them dance this version."

2791
01:45:26,730 --> 01:45:27,730
I'm sure of it.

2792
01:45:27,930 --> 01:45:30,100
I was a bit disappointed.

2793
01:45:30,330 --> 01:45:31,430
Would it be okay...

2794
01:45:31,560 --> 01:45:32,999
if you didn't read the paper now?

2795
01:45:33,000 --> 01:45:35,529
(The concept paper was handed out in advance.)

2796
01:45:35,530 --> 01:45:38,800
Could I go over the presentation slides first?

2797
01:45:39,270 --> 01:45:40,270
Presentation slides?

2798
01:45:41,640 --> 01:45:44,279
We're on a tight schedule. When on earth...

2799
01:45:44,280 --> 01:45:45,639
did she put together the slides?

2800
01:45:45,640 --> 01:45:47,849
I can only imagine just how much work she put into this.

2801
01:45:47,850 --> 01:45:49,650
This is the Title Sequence Film Mission.

2802
01:45:49,720 --> 01:45:51,049
I'm sure everyone did...

2803
01:45:51,050 --> 01:45:52,619
a great job with the video.

2804
01:45:52,620 --> 01:45:54,589
First of all, for this Film Mission,

2805
01:45:54,590 --> 01:45:57,660
I believe that the concept matters the most.

2806
01:45:57,890 --> 01:45:59,489
With that in mind, I decided on...

2807
01:45:59,490 --> 01:46:00,930
"The Matrix."

2808
01:46:02,560 --> 01:46:05,829
When I heard that she chose "The Matrix" for her concept,

2809
01:46:05,830 --> 01:46:07,770
I thought it was original and sounded fun.

2810
01:46:07,870 --> 01:46:09,870
She's a genius when it comes to crafting concepts.

2811
01:46:09,900 --> 01:46:11,970
I really wanted to steal her concept.

2812
01:46:12,070 --> 01:46:13,539
Deciding on the narrative took more time...

2813
01:46:13,540 --> 01:46:15,020
than coming up with the choreography.

2814
01:46:15,940 --> 01:46:16,940
It's perfect.

2815
01:46:16,941 --> 01:46:18,786
I decided to go with "The Matrix" as my concept.

2816
01:46:18,810 --> 01:46:19,810
This is it.

2817
01:46:19,811 --> 01:46:21,409
It suits my choreography style.

2818
01:46:21,410 --> 01:46:23,420
And it's going to look amazing.

2819
01:46:23,720 --> 01:46:25,650
It's just the perfect choice across the board.

2820
01:46:25,850 --> 01:46:27,519
When I thought of the movie, a few colors came to mind.

2821
01:46:27,520 --> 01:46:29,049
Metal, black, and green.

2822
01:46:29,050 --> 01:46:30,360
Those are my key colors.

2823
01:46:30,420 --> 01:46:32,119
This is my mood board.

2824
01:46:32,120 --> 01:46:33,766
I feel very confident when it comes to styling.

2825
01:46:33,790 --> 01:46:34,930
I agree. Yes.

2826
01:46:34,960 --> 01:46:36,106
Her styling for "Avatar" was great.

2827
01:46:36,130 --> 01:46:37,230
It was incredible.

2828
01:46:37,460 --> 01:46:39,099
Simeez's presentation was...

2829
01:46:39,100 --> 01:46:40,329
by far the best.

2830
01:46:40,330 --> 01:46:41,399
"This is the vibe."

2831
01:46:41,400 --> 01:46:42,469
"This is the mood board."

2832
01:46:42,470 --> 01:46:44,369
"Here are the key points."

2833
01:46:44,370 --> 01:46:46,770
She prepared her presentation to persuade us.

2834
01:46:46,840 --> 01:46:47,969
My gosh. I really thought...

2835
01:46:47,970 --> 01:46:49,239
she was going to win this.

2836
01:46:49,240 --> 01:46:51,516
I was determined to become the director for this mission.

2837
01:46:51,540 --> 01:46:53,950
Let's watch my choreography video now.

2838
01:46:54,010 --> 01:46:55,850
I was expecting something amazing.

2839
01:46:57,420 --> 01:46:58,649
I can't wait.

2840
01:46:58,650 --> 01:47:00,330
(Choreography Concept Credit Board Simeez)

2841
01:47:02,050 --> 01:47:03,690
Emma is in the video.

2842
01:47:09,830 --> 01:47:11,260
She went with five girls.

2843
01:47:12,230 --> 01:47:15,100
She did a good job bringing out my dance style.

2844
01:47:18,070 --> 01:47:19,370
I can pull that off, right?

2845
01:47:23,880 --> 01:47:25,009
You have to keep dancing.

2846
01:47:25,010 --> 01:47:26,650
Right. I have to keep dancing.

2847
01:47:28,150 --> 01:47:29,819
Some parts of the choreograph fell short.

2848
01:47:29,820 --> 01:47:31,520
She hasn't grasped my style as a dancer.

2849
01:47:33,350 --> 01:47:36,049
A few of those moves came across twerking.

2850
01:47:36,050 --> 01:47:37,590
I was a bit worried about that.

2851
01:47:39,760 --> 01:47:41,659
I didn't see much dancing on the staircase.

2852
01:47:41,660 --> 01:47:43,660
The choreography felt a bit hollow.

2853
01:47:46,400 --> 01:47:47,669
I'm always on my knees.

2854
01:47:47,670 --> 01:47:48,869
(Feeling guilty, laughing)

2855
01:47:48,870 --> 01:47:50,299
I guess that's in every choreography.

2856
01:47:50,300 --> 01:47:51,540
That must be MIN JUN's thing.

2857
01:47:53,170 --> 01:47:55,010
It looked unique and fun.

2858
01:47:58,840 --> 01:48:00,450
Why did Simeez dance for my part?

2859
01:48:00,510 --> 01:48:02,849
It was the first time...

2860
01:48:02,850 --> 01:48:05,719
I've ever seen Simeez take on a male part.

2861
01:48:05,720 --> 01:48:07,520
That change was quite refreshing. I liked it.

2862
01:48:10,690 --> 01:48:14,359
(You can watch Simeez's full video on "The CHOOM" and "Mnet Plus.")

2863
01:48:14,360 --> 01:48:15,760
As soon as I watched the video,

2864
01:48:15,960 --> 01:48:18,229
I felt that her choreography didn't quite live up...

2865
01:48:18,230 --> 01:48:19,800
to her presentation.

2866
01:48:19,900 --> 01:48:21,929
It made me wonder why she chose "The Matrix."

2867
01:48:21,930 --> 01:48:23,129
It was disappointing...

2868
01:48:23,130 --> 01:48:25,069
that the choreography didn't connect to the concept.

2869
01:48:25,070 --> 01:48:26,769
The choreography had nothing to do...

2870
01:48:26,770 --> 01:48:27,809
with the concept.

2871
01:48:27,810 --> 01:48:29,470
When I was listening to her presentation,

2872
01:48:29,540 --> 01:48:30,939
I thought her pitch was really cool...

2873
01:48:30,940 --> 01:48:32,409
and she was super professional.

2874
01:48:32,410 --> 01:48:33,679
I thought it was going to be great.

2875
01:48:33,680 --> 01:48:34,850
But when I watched the video,

2876
01:48:35,050 --> 01:48:36,410
I was like, "What? What's this?"

2877
01:48:36,510 --> 01:48:39,649
They didn't seem to match.

2878
01:48:39,650 --> 01:48:41,250
Where's the connection to "The Matrix?"

2879
01:48:41,290 --> 01:48:42,789
Which part of the routine is supposed to fit the concept?

2880
01:48:42,790 --> 01:48:44,259
I kept getting these questions in my head.

2881
01:48:44,260 --> 01:48:45,819
Only after watching my first draft,

2882
01:48:45,820 --> 01:48:47,659
she commented that she didn't see how "The Matrix" fit in.

2883
01:48:47,660 --> 01:48:49,190
This shows how limited her view is.

2884
01:48:49,290 --> 01:48:51,460
Which part are you exactly referring to?

2885
01:48:51,530 --> 01:48:52,559
I don't get it.

2886
01:48:52,560 --> 01:48:53,869
If your choreography...

2887
01:48:53,870 --> 01:48:55,199
fit the concept better...

2888
01:48:55,200 --> 01:48:56,200
and was more convincing enough...

2889
01:48:56,201 --> 01:48:57,239
But...

2890
01:48:57,240 --> 01:48:59,099
this video is only a draft.

2891
01:48:59,100 --> 01:49:02,039
Telling me that you didn't capture the concept enough...

2892
01:49:02,040 --> 01:49:04,109
only after watching this is a bit too much...

2893
01:49:04,110 --> 01:49:05,139
in my opinion.

2894
01:49:05,140 --> 01:49:06,910
I was quite flustered.

2895
01:49:06,950 --> 01:49:07,950
Why?

2896
01:49:07,951 --> 01:49:09,849
At the end of the day, the video...

2897
01:49:09,850 --> 01:49:11,419
has to be enough to express the concept.

2898
01:49:11,420 --> 01:49:12,549
But if the video can't do that,

2899
01:49:12,550 --> 01:49:14,250
it means she failed, doesn't it?

2900
01:49:14,450 --> 01:49:16,689
This is my personal opinion. This was supposed to be a film.

2901
01:49:16,690 --> 01:49:19,219
When filming the choreography video as a draft for a K-pop artist,

2902
01:49:19,220 --> 01:49:20,729
I'm not a fan...

2903
01:49:20,730 --> 01:49:22,159
of using a wide-angle lens...

2904
01:49:22,160 --> 01:49:24,760
to direct the front-and-back movements.

2905
01:49:24,900 --> 01:49:26,630
The atmosphere felt ice-cold.

2906
01:49:27,730 --> 01:49:28,829
What is this?

2907
01:49:28,830 --> 01:49:31,169
It was a film, so I expected to see cinematic directions.

2908
01:49:31,170 --> 01:49:32,799
They just moved around the gimbal.

2909
01:49:32,800 --> 01:49:34,469
There were a few camera transitions.

2910
01:49:34,470 --> 01:49:36,309
Her video pretty much followed...

2911
01:49:36,310 --> 01:49:39,010
the typical format of K-pop choreography videos.

2912
01:49:39,950 --> 01:49:41,449
I can go on and on about K-pop...

2913
01:49:41,450 --> 01:49:43,449
since that's the industry I work in.

2914
01:49:43,450 --> 01:49:44,619
But...

2915
01:49:44,620 --> 01:49:47,350
it sounded like he was looking down on K-pop.

2916
01:49:47,520 --> 01:49:48,820
I just don't get it.

2917
01:49:48,890 --> 01:49:50,059
"How could he look down on it?"

2918
01:49:50,060 --> 01:49:51,519
"And he's young too."

2919
01:49:51,520 --> 01:49:53,120
(He's young too.)

2920
01:49:53,690 --> 01:49:54,989
Kasper,

2921
01:49:54,990 --> 01:49:57,160
please give out your concept paper.

2922
01:49:58,330 --> 01:50:01,269
(INGYOO checks the concept paper.)

2923
01:50:01,270 --> 01:50:02,700
(Gasping)

2924
01:50:02,800 --> 01:50:04,069
(Shocked)

2925
01:50:04,070 --> 01:50:05,170
What's this?

2926
01:50:05,440 --> 01:50:06,440
What is it?

2927
01:50:06,570 --> 01:50:08,840
My goodness. What's this?

2928
01:50:09,170 --> 01:50:10,310
No way.

2929
01:50:10,380 --> 01:50:11,709
- "The Matrix." - My goodness.

2930
01:50:11,710 --> 01:50:13,450
- It's the same concept. - This is fun.

2931
01:50:13,810 --> 01:50:15,949
My concept is super strong.

2932
01:50:15,950 --> 01:50:17,949
I don't think my concept...

2933
01:50:17,950 --> 01:50:19,819
- will overlap with anyone's. - It's perfect.

2934
01:50:19,820 --> 01:50:21,719
(During her concept presentation)

2935
01:50:21,720 --> 01:50:22,849
("The Matrix")

2936
01:50:22,850 --> 01:50:26,930
(He saw that she chose the same concept as him.)

2937
01:50:27,390 --> 01:50:28,930
"My gosh. Look at her."

2938
01:50:29,330 --> 01:50:31,660
"We're not so different." That's what I thought.

2939
01:50:31,730 --> 01:50:34,129
Coincidentally, Hee Jung and I...

2940
01:50:34,130 --> 01:50:36,499
chose the same concept for this mission.

2941
01:50:36,500 --> 01:50:38,439
But our interpretation is different.

2942
01:50:38,440 --> 01:50:39,669
So keep that in mind.

2943
01:50:39,670 --> 01:50:41,439
He took the opposite direction...

2944
01:50:41,440 --> 01:50:43,139
to capture this concept, "The Matrix."

2945
01:50:43,140 --> 01:50:46,309
Simeez worked really hard to visualize the concept...

2946
01:50:46,310 --> 01:50:47,726
and incorporate it into his choreography.

2947
01:50:47,750 --> 01:50:50,549
When taking on this mission,

2948
01:50:50,550 --> 01:50:53,620
I wanted to maximize everyone's character.

2949
01:50:53,650 --> 01:50:55,189
In my piece,

2950
01:50:55,190 --> 01:50:57,160
INGYOO is...

2951
01:50:58,090 --> 01:50:59,490
the main character.

2952
01:51:00,390 --> 01:51:03,159
(Me?)

2953
01:51:03,160 --> 01:51:06,000
(Why INGYOO, all of a sudden?)

2954
01:51:06,100 --> 01:51:08,930
Kasper isn't sought-after as a choreography in the industry.

2955
01:51:09,000 --> 01:51:10,439
It's like...

2956
01:51:10,440 --> 01:51:13,040
he's buying a new product at an outlet.

2957
01:51:13,100 --> 01:51:15,570
The bad blood between INGYOO and Kasper is real.

2958
01:51:15,840 --> 01:51:17,180
He's the main character.

2959
01:51:17,210 --> 01:51:19,140
It felt nice.

2960
01:51:20,150 --> 01:51:21,750
So INGYOO...

2961
01:51:21,850 --> 01:51:23,949
will be portraying the system error in the choreography.

2962
01:51:23,950 --> 01:51:26,320
(A system error)

2963
01:51:26,420 --> 01:51:27,750
A system error.

2964
01:51:28,490 --> 01:51:29,720
You are one in real life too.

2965
01:51:29,820 --> 01:51:32,259
I liked that it captured my position on this show.

2966
01:51:32,260 --> 01:51:33,789
I'm like a glitch on this show.

2967
01:51:33,790 --> 01:51:36,270
I do some things on this show that make me look like a glitch.

2968
01:51:36,560 --> 01:51:38,699
INGYOO has the bad boy position on the show.

2969
01:51:38,700 --> 01:51:40,399
Everyone would agree with this concept.

2970
01:51:40,400 --> 01:51:42,400
This kind of idea is fun.

2971
01:51:42,430 --> 01:51:44,299
He's going to be the system error.

2972
01:51:44,300 --> 01:51:46,639
I did my best to portray his arrogance...

2973
01:51:46,640 --> 01:51:47,810
in the video.

2974
01:51:48,410 --> 01:51:51,140
(Choreography Concept Credit Board)

2975
01:51:52,610 --> 01:51:54,709
(It's not on pause.)

2976
01:51:54,710 --> 01:51:56,350
What's going on? What is it?

2977
01:51:56,710 --> 01:51:59,149
The entire intro was just blank.

2978
01:51:59,150 --> 01:52:01,349
I think the intro plays a crucial role.

2979
01:52:01,350 --> 01:52:02,889
Those ten seconds are so precious.

2980
01:52:02,890 --> 01:52:04,660
That was the most disappointing part.

2981
01:52:08,160 --> 01:52:09,659
The choreography had...

2982
01:52:09,660 --> 01:52:11,429
unique movements.

2983
01:52:11,430 --> 01:52:12,960
I couldn't stop watching.

2984
01:52:13,600 --> 01:52:15,030
I guess that's me.

2985
01:52:16,630 --> 01:52:18,300
He even utilized the lighting.

2986
01:52:19,100 --> 01:52:20,669
That does look fun.

2987
01:52:20,670 --> 01:52:22,040
Koo Young and MIN JUN.

2988
01:52:24,980 --> 01:52:27,050
I thought it'd be fun to do that with Simeez.

2989
01:52:29,150 --> 01:52:30,150
(The 2nd system error)

2990
01:52:30,151 --> 01:52:33,819
He picked a good color for the lighting that fit the mood.

2991
01:52:33,820 --> 01:52:35,820
Setting the mood is all about the lighting.

2992
01:52:38,920 --> 01:52:40,630
- Who's that? - It's BABYZOO.

2993
01:52:40,760 --> 01:52:42,530
(It's BABYZOO's part.)

2994
01:52:43,060 --> 01:52:44,160
(The 3rd system error)

2995
01:52:46,260 --> 01:52:47,830
He skipped adding any moves here.

2996
01:52:49,130 --> 01:52:50,369
But that's pretty cool.

2997
01:52:50,370 --> 01:52:52,900
He went with such bold decisions.

2998
01:52:56,510 --> 01:52:58,610
I liked the move for the breathing part.

2999
01:53:04,350 --> 01:53:06,220
(The system error is satisfied with it.)

3000
01:53:06,320 --> 01:53:08,040
The choreography for the chorus is amazing.

3001
01:53:08,120 --> 01:53:09,320
It's good, isn't it?

3002
01:53:09,620 --> 01:53:10,720
(It goes like this.)

3003
01:53:11,490 --> 01:53:12,859
I wanted to steal the choreography for the chorus.

3004
01:53:12,860 --> 01:53:14,460
It was super catchy.

3005
01:53:14,560 --> 01:53:15,659
I liked your bold decision...

3006
01:53:15,660 --> 01:53:19,160
to keep the choreography for the chorus simple.

3007
01:53:19,330 --> 01:53:21,399
I thought assigning me the system error as my role...

3008
01:53:21,400 --> 01:53:23,299
could be a secret weapon...

3009
01:53:23,300 --> 01:53:25,940
compared to the other draft we saw earlier.

3010
01:53:26,040 --> 01:53:27,369
Your use of lighting...

3011
01:53:27,370 --> 01:53:29,470
made the concept click for the audience.

3012
01:53:29,540 --> 01:53:30,679
When you think of the movie,

3013
01:53:30,680 --> 01:53:31,809
you'd think of the red pill and the blue pill.

3014
01:53:31,810 --> 01:53:33,679
Integrating that as the main theme...

3015
01:53:33,680 --> 01:53:36,050
made sense in terms of props.

3016
01:53:36,550 --> 01:53:38,120
This is so disappointing.

3017
01:53:38,150 --> 01:53:40,420
It'd be crazy if mine doesn't get chosen.

3018
01:53:40,520 --> 01:53:41,790
I'm super confident.

3019
01:53:41,920 --> 01:53:43,559
I have a question.

3020
01:53:43,560 --> 01:53:45,319
When transitioning into the group choreography,

3021
01:53:45,320 --> 01:53:47,689
everyone stays still.

3022
01:53:47,690 --> 01:53:49,329
Five, six, seven, eight.

3023
01:53:49,330 --> 01:53:50,359
One, two, three...

3024
01:53:50,360 --> 01:53:51,759
He has to build up the momentum all over again.

3025
01:53:51,760 --> 01:53:53,769
If he wants that to be the highlight,

3026
01:53:53,770 --> 01:53:55,499
the formation has to go from messy to neat.

3027
01:53:55,500 --> 01:53:57,669
I think that approach is more appropriate for this.

3028
01:53:57,670 --> 01:53:58,900
But it wasn't.

3029
01:53:59,170 --> 01:54:02,010
I'm most curious why you didn't go with the opposite flow.

3030
01:54:02,310 --> 01:54:03,679
I didn't get it.

3031
01:54:03,680 --> 01:54:04,879
MIN JUN and I...

3032
01:54:04,880 --> 01:54:06,139
just focus on different things.

3033
01:54:06,140 --> 01:54:07,179
Our views are different.

3034
01:54:07,180 --> 01:54:08,180
First of all...

3035
01:54:08,181 --> 01:54:09,249
The thing is that,

3036
01:54:09,250 --> 01:54:11,096
I come with choreography that they want to dance.

3037
01:54:11,120 --> 01:54:12,919
- The chorus choreography is great. - It is, isn't it?

3038
01:54:12,920 --> 01:54:15,250
That was my priority.

3039
01:54:15,290 --> 01:54:16,320
But...

3040
01:54:16,350 --> 01:54:18,020
he asked me this ridiculous question.

3041
01:54:18,420 --> 01:54:20,206
I had the most difficult time understanding that.

3042
01:54:20,230 --> 01:54:22,259
This is the Title Sequence Film Mission.

3043
01:54:22,260 --> 01:54:24,206
The artistic quality of the video looked a bit iffy.

3044
01:54:24,230 --> 01:54:25,700
What about yours then?

3045
01:54:25,900 --> 01:54:27,600
MIN JUN has strong opinions...

3046
01:54:27,630 --> 01:54:29,499
and a strong personality.

3047
01:54:29,500 --> 01:54:31,180
He has a lot of ideas he wants to express.

3048
01:54:31,240 --> 01:54:32,299
He was...

3049
01:54:32,300 --> 01:54:33,339
just...

3050
01:54:33,340 --> 01:54:34,970
attacking my choreography.

3051
01:54:35,270 --> 01:54:36,910
I'm a bit flustered.

3052
01:54:37,110 --> 01:54:38,280
MIN JUN.

3053
01:54:38,340 --> 01:54:39,810
Let's check yours out then.

3054
01:54:39,840 --> 01:54:42,349
(The fourth choreographer to present the concept and video)

3055
01:54:42,350 --> 01:54:44,949
(JEONG MIN JUN)

3056
01:54:44,950 --> 01:54:47,249
I'm up against nine choreographers in this mission.

3057
01:54:47,250 --> 01:54:48,719
There's this pressure...

3058
01:54:48,720 --> 01:54:50,866
that I should be the director and put out a great piece.

3059
01:54:50,890 --> 01:54:52,360
I have to stand out.

3060
01:54:52,460 --> 01:54:54,629
As soon as I heard the song,

3061
01:54:54,630 --> 01:54:56,460
the movie, "The Thieves," came to mind.

3062
01:54:56,730 --> 01:54:59,759
And the bomb scene orchestrated by the Joker...

3063
01:54:59,760 --> 01:55:02,630
in "The Dark Knight" came to mind too.

3064
01:55:03,330 --> 01:55:04,639
Let's see if yours looks like a film.

3065
01:55:04,640 --> 01:55:05,800
Let's see how good you are.

3066
01:55:05,900 --> 01:55:08,069
It's called the Title Sequence Film Mission.

3067
01:55:08,070 --> 01:55:09,870
It will be the title sequence of the show.

3068
01:55:09,940 --> 01:55:13,580
Taking a cinematic approach would give me an edge.

3069
01:55:13,780 --> 01:55:16,109
The directors show up in a car.

3070
01:55:16,110 --> 01:55:18,119
Then they share the blueprint and the plan.

3071
01:55:18,120 --> 01:55:20,049
As BADA gets out of the car,

3072
01:55:20,050 --> 01:55:21,249
she puts on a timer on the car.

3073
01:55:21,250 --> 01:55:23,090
But that's a timer for the dynamite.

3074
01:55:23,420 --> 01:55:25,019
I'm looking forward to watch his video.

3075
01:55:25,020 --> 01:55:26,700
I'm curious as to how he'll play this out.

3076
01:55:26,920 --> 01:55:29,359
Toward the end of the story, we see the bomb on the car.

3077
01:55:29,360 --> 01:55:31,899
Just when the ten of us are about to throw something...

3078
01:55:31,900 --> 01:55:33,769
at the building in the back,

3079
01:55:33,770 --> 01:55:35,090
the building is going to explode.

3080
01:55:35,600 --> 01:55:37,800
That's the kind of direction I'm hoping to stage.

3081
01:55:38,000 --> 01:55:39,639
I think his goal was...

3082
01:55:39,640 --> 01:55:43,009
to give a very cinematic touch to his video.

3083
01:55:43,010 --> 01:55:44,439
It will be fun to film this.

3084
01:55:44,440 --> 01:55:47,049
I knew it. MIN JUN is the king of storylines.

3085
01:55:47,050 --> 01:55:48,250
This is why I lost to him.

3086
01:55:48,510 --> 01:55:50,750
If I'm not the director in this mission,

3087
01:55:50,920 --> 01:55:51,920
I'll just be a dancer.

3088
01:55:52,120 --> 01:55:54,020
I wanted to be the director.

3089
01:55:54,690 --> 01:55:55,790
I can't wait to watch it.

3090
01:55:56,390 --> 01:55:57,490
I had high expectations.

3091
01:55:57,620 --> 01:55:59,166
Honestly, I didn't expect much from him.

3092
01:55:59,190 --> 01:56:01,130
I don't think I'll like it, but I was curious.

3093
01:56:01,690 --> 01:56:03,999
(Title Sequence Film Mission)

3094
01:56:04,000 --> 01:56:06,260
(Choreography Concept Credit Board)

3095
01:56:07,100 --> 01:56:09,129
(The choreographers show up in a car.)

3096
01:56:09,130 --> 01:56:11,169
(BADA gets out of the car.)

3097
01:56:11,170 --> 01:56:12,240
It's Piki.

3098
01:56:12,570 --> 01:56:15,810
(She puts the timer for the dynamite on the car.)

3099
01:56:16,510 --> 01:56:19,509
(The choreographers enter the building.)

3100
01:56:19,510 --> 01:56:24,350
(They carry out their own tasks.)

3101
01:56:27,320 --> 01:56:28,519
He focused more on the cinematic aspect,

3102
01:56:28,520 --> 01:56:30,460
- not the choreography. - Yes. Totally.

3103
01:56:36,030 --> 01:56:38,960
The storyline he had in mind didn't come through in the video.

3104
01:56:43,070 --> 01:56:45,599
It would've been neater...

3105
01:56:45,600 --> 01:56:47,610
if we didn't see them bringing the mirror.

3106
01:56:52,480 --> 01:56:54,910
The transitions weren't my style.

3107
01:56:57,550 --> 01:56:59,350
That's supposed to be a running scene, right?

3108
01:57:01,550 --> 01:57:03,589
Which part of this film is supposed to...

3109
01:57:03,590 --> 01:57:05,059
remind us of "The Thieves?"

3110
01:57:05,060 --> 01:57:06,500
I didn't see the motif in the video.

3111
01:57:13,260 --> 01:57:14,776
Given the lengthy explanation he gave us,

3112
01:57:14,800 --> 01:57:16,870
his video lacked substance. It was disappointing.

3113
01:57:19,370 --> 01:57:21,569
I got the feeling that it was very one-dimensional.

3114
01:57:21,570 --> 01:57:23,040
I only remember seeing the dance.

3115
01:57:25,610 --> 01:57:27,780
(The 10 choreographers blow up the building.)

3116
01:57:29,650 --> 01:57:30,920
Personally, I was disappointed.

3117
01:57:31,550 --> 01:57:33,710
I watched it while picturing it as the title sequence.

3118
01:57:33,750 --> 01:57:35,619
The problem was that...

3119
01:57:35,620 --> 01:57:37,620
it sort of turned out half-baked.

3120
01:57:38,790 --> 01:57:41,389
Contrary to what you promised us, the video wasn't...

3121
01:57:41,390 --> 01:57:43,630
convincing enough for your idea to come through.

3122
01:57:45,000 --> 01:57:46,160
Gosh, he's so scary.

3123
01:57:48,230 --> 01:57:50,499
You gave us a lengthy presentation.

3124
01:57:50,500 --> 01:57:52,969
You used the car for the countdown.

3125
01:57:52,970 --> 01:57:54,139
At the end, we throw something,

3126
01:57:54,140 --> 01:57:56,409
and the bomb explodes. So the building blows up.

3127
01:57:56,410 --> 01:57:59,180
I don't quite understand how the middle part fits in here.

3128
01:58:00,240 --> 01:58:01,810
This is the title sequence?

3129
01:58:02,410 --> 01:58:04,770
The more I thought about it, the less it worked in my head.

3130
01:58:05,320 --> 01:58:08,490
He made it sound like he planned a lot for it,

3131
01:58:08,590 --> 01:58:09,790
but it didn't come through.

3132
01:58:10,150 --> 01:58:12,889
"I've been thinking a lot about it for as long as I can remember."

3133
01:58:12,890 --> 01:58:14,359
"I gave it a lot of thought."

3134
01:58:14,360 --> 01:58:16,359
"I had to go abroad and even make a transfer."

3135
01:58:16,360 --> 01:58:18,199
"Once I landed, it took me a three-hour ride to get there."

3136
01:58:18,200 --> 01:58:20,059
"Then I went through all sorts of trouble to find this."

3137
01:58:20,060 --> 01:58:22,076
"Afterward, I brought it back to Korea with utmost care."

3138
01:58:22,100 --> 01:58:23,176
"This is the instant rice."

3139
01:58:23,200 --> 01:58:24,400
That's how it felt.

3140
01:58:25,300 --> 01:58:28,509
What he promised us and the video didn't match.

3141
01:58:28,510 --> 01:58:29,940
That must've been why.

3142
01:58:30,340 --> 01:58:32,109
After watching his video, it was obvious that...

3143
01:58:32,110 --> 01:58:34,550
he had limited experience in working with other teams.

3144
01:58:34,710 --> 01:58:36,110
Can I be brutally honest?

3145
01:58:36,410 --> 01:58:38,920
It looked like a midterm project from a college student.

3146
01:58:39,520 --> 01:58:40,720
(I see.)

3147
01:58:41,750 --> 01:58:43,249
My college assignments...

3148
01:58:43,250 --> 01:58:44,789
used to look exactly like that.

3149
01:58:44,790 --> 01:58:46,259
The story itself was substantial.

3150
01:58:46,260 --> 01:58:48,890
But he just ended up filming in different places.

3151
01:58:49,090 --> 01:58:52,030
If this were a college assignment, I would've given him an A plus.

3152
01:58:52,130 --> 01:58:54,330
But this is Street World Fighter: Directors' War.

3153
01:58:54,670 --> 01:58:56,499
For that to be the title sequence,

3154
01:58:56,500 --> 01:59:01,210
his film failed to convey the identity of the show.

3155
01:59:01,740 --> 01:59:04,156
Anyone who can understand my intention would instantly get it.

3156
01:59:04,180 --> 01:59:06,340
But a lot of them didn't get it.

3157
01:59:06,540 --> 01:59:08,310
So that was frustrating.

3158
01:59:08,450 --> 01:59:10,450
I don't think you did a good job...

3159
01:59:10,650 --> 01:59:12,226
of bringing each dancer's character to life.

3160
01:59:12,250 --> 01:59:13,619
The lyrics went, "Nod your head."

3161
01:59:13,620 --> 01:59:15,350
So that's what he did, and I hated it.

3162
01:59:15,720 --> 01:59:16,720
(Nod your head)

3163
01:59:16,721 --> 01:59:18,360
I hate one-dimensional approaches.

3164
01:59:18,490 --> 01:59:20,730
As for my part,

3165
01:59:21,260 --> 01:59:24,930
you included the type of move I liked the least.

3166
01:59:25,600 --> 01:59:28,429
Even before doing this mission, this was the type of role...

3167
01:59:28,430 --> 01:59:30,270
I considered the worst for me.

3168
01:59:30,430 --> 01:59:32,240
I did a few turns and did a jump.

3169
01:59:33,370 --> 01:59:34,440
It was shocking.

3170
01:59:36,610 --> 01:59:39,810
I'm not a dancer who can just do turns and jumps.

3171
01:59:40,010 --> 01:59:41,649
(Shocked)

3172
01:59:41,650 --> 01:59:43,350
That was quite disappointing.

3173
01:59:44,520 --> 01:59:46,019
MIN JUN failed to understand her style.

3174
01:59:46,020 --> 01:59:47,120
- Right. - Yes.

3175
01:59:48,290 --> 01:59:49,290
Thank you.

3176
01:59:49,920 --> 01:59:51,060
(Surprised)

3177
01:59:51,490 --> 01:59:52,560
(Shocked)

3178
01:59:52,960 --> 01:59:54,090
I was quite surprised.

3179
01:59:54,230 --> 01:59:55,390
It caught me off guard.

3180
01:59:55,690 --> 01:59:57,759
(The choreographers are flustered after seeing her concept paper.)

3181
01:59:57,760 --> 01:59:59,030
I was fascinated.

3182
01:59:59,200 --> 02:00:01,570
Let me go over my concept first.

3183
02:00:02,100 --> 02:00:04,840
My concept is The Heist.

3184
02:00:05,440 --> 02:00:08,540
BADA had the same concept as me.

3185
02:00:08,870 --> 02:00:10,680
(His concept was "The Thieves.")

3186
02:00:11,380 --> 02:00:12,410
I'm doomed.

3187
02:00:12,840 --> 02:00:14,109
(BADA chose the same concept as MIN JUN which is "The Thieves.")

3188
02:00:14,110 --> 02:00:15,249
(BADA chose the same concept as MIN JUN which is "The Thieves.")

3189
02:00:15,250 --> 02:00:16,350
It was shocking.

3190
02:00:17,010 --> 02:00:19,220
- We're thieves. - Gosh. This is crazy.

3191
02:00:19,620 --> 02:00:21,720
So those two picked "The Thieves" for their concept.

3192
02:00:21,990 --> 02:00:25,090
I was really shocked because MIN JUN and I chose...

3193
02:00:25,290 --> 02:00:26,490
the same concept.

3194
02:00:27,330 --> 02:00:29,290
As soon as I saw his concept,

3195
02:00:29,460 --> 02:00:31,220
my mind went blank. I thought, "I'm doomed."

3196
02:00:32,360 --> 02:00:33,760
It's the same concept.

3197
02:00:34,300 --> 02:00:37,770
I thought I was the only one who came up with this idea.

3198
02:00:37,940 --> 02:00:40,000
"No!"

3199
02:00:40,270 --> 02:00:42,340
"Oh, no. This is mine."

3200
02:00:42,670 --> 02:00:45,240
I thought about ways to make my presentation stand out.

3201
02:00:45,610 --> 02:00:48,209
So I was going to make sure my concept came through.

3202
02:00:48,210 --> 02:00:51,549
I thought our show was about keeping what's yours...

3203
02:00:51,550 --> 02:00:53,819
while trying to steal someone else's.

3204
02:00:53,820 --> 02:00:55,266
I wanted to make good use of the props.

3205
02:00:55,290 --> 02:00:58,389
This treasure box is the main visual element and key point.

3206
02:00:58,390 --> 02:01:00,359
I'm going to build the routine...

3207
02:01:00,360 --> 02:01:03,290
from the staging to choreography around this treasure box.

3208
02:01:03,430 --> 02:01:05,160
I wanted my choreography to stand out.

3209
02:01:05,300 --> 02:01:06,906
This is the move when the song goes, "royalty."

3210
02:01:06,930 --> 02:01:08,829
(BADA's signature dance move)

3211
02:01:08,830 --> 02:01:10,070
So something like this.

3212
02:01:10,200 --> 02:01:11,899
(The catchy dance move...)

3213
02:01:11,900 --> 02:01:14,039
(makes them try it out right away.)

3214
02:01:14,040 --> 02:01:15,040
Oh, my neck.

3215
02:01:15,041 --> 02:01:18,340
It was nice. But to be honest,

3216
02:01:18,480 --> 02:01:19,809
the concept is too plain.

3217
02:01:19,810 --> 02:01:21,450
Everyone's done the heist concept before.

3218
02:01:21,550 --> 02:01:24,519
(BADA and MIN JUN's concept: "The Thieves")

3219
02:01:24,520 --> 02:01:26,019
I can't even count...

3220
02:01:26,020 --> 02:01:28,249
how many performances I created around the heist concept. I mean it.

3221
02:01:28,250 --> 02:01:31,459
THE BOYZ released a song called...

3222
02:01:31,460 --> 02:01:32,559
"The Stealer."

3223
02:01:32,560 --> 02:01:34,330
(THE BOYZ's song, "The Stealer")

3224
02:01:34,390 --> 02:01:37,190
They performed the song at nine different awards ceremonies.

3225
02:01:37,400 --> 02:01:40,159
I came up with 9 performances in 2 months with the same concept.

3226
02:01:40,160 --> 02:01:41,429
The setups were all different.

3227
02:01:41,430 --> 02:01:43,706
I've done all kinds of things with this concept. Seriously.

3228
02:01:43,730 --> 02:01:46,469
(The master of the heist concept, Back Koo Young)

3229
02:01:46,470 --> 02:01:49,440
Personally, I'm sick of this heist concept.

3230
02:01:49,640 --> 02:01:52,480
If they're going to use this concept for the title sequence film,

3231
02:01:52,710 --> 02:01:56,110
it has to be a lot more elaborate. If they can pull this off,

3232
02:01:56,350 --> 02:01:59,150
I would be able to treat it as a title sequence film.

3233
02:01:59,720 --> 02:02:01,049
It was the same concept as mine.

3234
02:02:01,050 --> 02:02:02,619
I was curious to see...

3235
02:02:02,620 --> 02:02:03,919
how her interpretation differed from mine.

3236
02:02:03,920 --> 02:02:05,320
(BADA's video is revealed.)

3237
02:02:05,720 --> 02:02:07,829
(Title Sequence Film Mission)

3238
02:02:07,830 --> 02:02:10,260
(Choreography Concept Credit Board)

3239
02:02:12,330 --> 02:02:13,899
(The master of the heist concept is looking forward to it.)

3240
02:02:13,900 --> 02:02:14,970
Oh, yes.

3241
02:02:24,140 --> 02:02:25,439
That's the role Shuri took.

3242
02:02:25,440 --> 02:02:26,510
Wait. Shuri?

3243
02:02:26,610 --> 02:02:28,450
This is a total betrayal, plain and simple.

3244
02:02:40,860 --> 02:02:44,229
She gave meaning to every single scene.

3245
02:02:44,230 --> 02:02:45,530
That was disappointing.

3246
02:02:50,200 --> 02:02:51,899
I saw a lot of moves...

3247
02:02:51,900 --> 02:02:53,300
I knew I could pull off well.

3248
02:02:54,710 --> 02:02:55,869
I thought her film was closer...

3249
02:02:55,870 --> 02:02:58,380
to matching the heist concept between the two.

3250
02:02:59,940 --> 02:03:02,649
I thought her choreography was neat and tight.

3251
02:03:02,650 --> 02:03:04,150
I liked it.

3252
02:03:11,320 --> 02:03:13,060
I liked her signature move.

3253
02:03:13,790 --> 02:03:14,829
(Getting hooked...)

3254
02:03:14,830 --> 02:03:15,960
(the second they see it)

3255
02:03:24,100 --> 02:03:25,100
I like this part.

3256
02:03:25,570 --> 02:03:27,069
The composition highlighted...

3257
02:03:27,070 --> 02:03:29,510
the lead choreographer and the secondary choreographer.

3258
02:03:38,220 --> 02:03:40,119
This will be the first video of the show.

3259
02:03:40,120 --> 02:03:42,120
This is going to be the face of the show in a way.

3260
02:03:42,250 --> 02:03:45,619
My focus in this mission was elevating the staging...

3261
02:03:45,620 --> 02:03:47,289
and cinematic quality...

3262
02:03:47,290 --> 02:03:49,690
while taking the choreography to the next level.

3263
02:03:50,290 --> 02:03:52,760
This clip won't show up in the middle of the competition.

3264
02:03:53,030 --> 02:03:55,930
It will be the title sequence. Considering that element,

3265
02:03:56,370 --> 02:04:00,470
MIN JUN's version was a bit light. So that was disappointing.

3266
02:04:00,940 --> 02:04:04,140
As for BADA's version, they had the same concept.

3267
02:04:04,280 --> 02:04:05,609
Looking at her choreography and setups,

3268
02:04:05,610 --> 02:04:07,309
I liked how some of her moves...

3269
02:04:07,310 --> 02:04:09,750
that really grounded the performance.

3270
02:04:09,950 --> 02:04:12,420
I saw some moves I knew I could deliver well.

3271
02:04:12,550 --> 02:04:13,819
(What did the master of the heist concept think?)

3272
02:04:13,820 --> 02:04:15,689
What's the point of telling you my opinion about BADA?

3273
02:04:15,690 --> 02:04:16,890
She's so good.

3274
02:04:17,320 --> 02:04:19,789
This heist concept is speaking to me now.

3275
02:04:19,790 --> 02:04:23,329
I liked that you continued using the prop until the end...

3276
02:04:23,330 --> 02:04:24,700
to keep the identity going.

3277
02:04:25,230 --> 02:04:29,530
If I were to assume that a trophy was in the treasure box,

3278
02:04:29,770 --> 02:04:33,570
utilizing it for the Title Sequence Film Mission...

3279
02:04:33,740 --> 02:04:36,210
would fit the objective. It worked well with the film.

3280
02:04:36,540 --> 02:04:38,639
It must be a direct result of her cinematic insight,

3281
02:04:38,640 --> 02:04:40,040
her understanding of this mission,

3282
02:04:40,180 --> 02:04:43,110
and her years of experience on large-scale projects.

3283
02:04:43,310 --> 02:04:44,819
It could very well be me.

3284
02:04:44,820 --> 02:04:47,049
It seemed like there was a glimmer of hope.

3285
02:04:47,050 --> 02:04:50,289
It makes me want to keep making...

3286
02:04:50,290 --> 02:04:51,290
the signature dance move.

3287
02:04:51,291 --> 02:04:53,060
I keep doing "Royalty."

3288
02:04:53,290 --> 02:04:55,089
- So... - What?

3289
02:04:55,090 --> 02:04:56,090
(Royalty)

3290
02:04:56,390 --> 02:04:58,329
This signature move is...

3291
02:04:58,330 --> 02:04:59,700
delicious.

3292
02:05:00,100 --> 02:05:02,130
Yummy. Is it because BADA did it?

3293
02:05:02,530 --> 02:05:06,799
Getting INGYOO to say something is delicious is truly like...

3294
02:05:06,800 --> 02:05:09,069
plucking a star from the sky.

3295
02:05:09,070 --> 02:05:11,309
I was really happy when he said the choreography...

3296
02:05:11,310 --> 02:05:12,879
for the chorus was delicious.

3297
02:05:12,880 --> 02:05:15,510
The downside is that each dancer has an assigned character.

3298
02:05:15,610 --> 02:05:19,020
(BADA assigned a specific character to each choreographer.)

3299
02:05:19,350 --> 02:05:22,319
It was difficult to capture the essence of the character...

3300
02:05:22,320 --> 02:05:25,089
and convey the intended meaning...

3301
02:05:25,090 --> 02:05:26,860
within such a brief scene.

3302
02:05:27,690 --> 02:05:28,729
In the first section,

3303
02:05:28,730 --> 02:05:30,689
only the treasure chest is visible, rather than people.

3304
02:05:30,690 --> 02:05:34,059
Trying to capture our dancing in such a short time,

3305
02:05:34,060 --> 02:05:35,669
it might actually get in the way.

3306
02:05:35,670 --> 02:05:37,129
It might feel a bit disappointing...

3307
02:05:37,130 --> 02:05:39,299
since the focus is on the treasure chest...

3308
02:05:39,300 --> 02:05:41,510
rather than people.

3309
02:05:42,370 --> 02:05:44,979
Leave the worrying about the props to me.

3310
02:05:44,980 --> 02:05:47,239
Give it to me as homework.

3311
02:05:47,240 --> 02:05:49,750
I think they'll pin a little hope on me.

3312
02:05:50,050 --> 02:05:52,049
Hash. Please come out.

3313
02:05:52,050 --> 02:05:54,126
(Presenting concept and draft video, the sixth choreographer Hash)

3314
02:05:54,150 --> 02:05:55,390
(Winking)

3315
02:05:56,090 --> 02:05:57,419
(Smiling)

3316
02:05:57,420 --> 02:06:00,519
Hash and I mostly competed against each other.

3317
02:06:00,520 --> 02:06:02,959
I have never directed...

3318
02:06:02,960 --> 02:06:05,229
a music video on my own.

3319
02:06:05,230 --> 02:06:08,830
But I was certain I possessed that sense.

3320
02:06:08,870 --> 02:06:12,369
Since this film serves to properly introduce...

3321
02:06:12,370 --> 02:06:14,439
the ten individuals...

3322
02:06:14,440 --> 02:06:17,169
in Street World Fighter: Director's War,

3323
02:06:17,170 --> 02:06:21,079
I wanted to craft a strong storyline.

3324
02:06:21,080 --> 02:06:22,909
I decided to let the atmosphere drive the narrative.

3325
02:06:22,910 --> 02:06:24,449
It's nice and simple.

3326
02:06:24,450 --> 02:06:26,749
It was similar to what I thought.

3327
02:06:26,750 --> 02:06:29,450
I appreciated her honesty in saying she wanted to keep it simple.

3328
02:06:29,920 --> 02:06:31,019
I think she did well.

3329
02:06:31,020 --> 02:06:32,260
(Agreeing)

3330
02:06:32,820 --> 02:06:34,960
(Choreography Concept Credit Board, Hash)

3331
02:06:35,330 --> 02:06:36,790
- This is going to be fun. - Yes.

3332
02:06:37,330 --> 02:06:39,030
It's cool.

3333
02:06:41,570 --> 02:06:43,070
The person playing me is really cool.

3334
02:06:45,040 --> 02:06:46,970
Simeez.

3335
02:06:50,840 --> 02:06:51,980
Cute.

3336
02:06:56,750 --> 02:06:58,620
Hash isn't Hash.

3337
02:07:03,950 --> 02:07:05,159
That's nice.

3338
02:07:05,160 --> 02:07:06,890
It was really innovative.

3339
02:07:09,960 --> 02:07:12,460
The choreography was very professional.

3340
02:07:13,300 --> 02:07:16,230
The variety of camera angles and fields of view was great.

3341
02:07:18,940 --> 02:07:20,039
This time you kneeled.

3342
02:07:20,040 --> 02:07:21,070
Right.

3343
02:07:22,470 --> 02:07:24,339
I wanted to see the chorus choreography,

3344
02:07:24,340 --> 02:07:26,409
but the screen suddenly split into three, so I couldn't see it.

3345
02:07:26,410 --> 02:07:27,910
It disrupted my concentration.

3346
02:07:29,950 --> 02:07:31,019
She's like Renan.

3347
02:07:31,020 --> 02:07:32,320
I thought it was Renan.

3348
02:07:39,960 --> 02:07:41,089
(Clapping)

3349
02:07:41,090 --> 02:07:42,830
(Satisfied)

3350
02:07:43,130 --> 02:07:45,659
The strength is the transition utilizing the glasses.

3351
02:07:45,660 --> 02:07:46,859
The eyeglass frame.

3352
02:07:46,860 --> 02:07:50,030
I liked the eyeglass frame because it was so fresh.

3353
02:07:50,170 --> 02:07:52,939
I thought the idea of having the dancers lying down...

3354
02:07:52,940 --> 02:07:56,639
be dragged away to express the music was a creative choice...

3355
02:07:56,640 --> 02:07:58,609
in terms of camera angles.

3356
02:07:58,610 --> 02:08:00,839
The shot where Renan is left behind...

3357
02:08:00,840 --> 02:08:04,849
looks a bit cute, but I wonder...

3358
02:08:04,850 --> 02:08:07,620
if it really matches her current image.

3359
02:08:07,920 --> 02:08:10,019
This video will be used for the opening.

3360
02:08:10,020 --> 02:08:12,919
Among all the videos I've seen so far,

3361
02:08:12,920 --> 02:08:16,389
it showcased the most diverse range of people within a minute.

3362
02:08:16,390 --> 02:08:18,799
You also put a lot of thought into how to utilize...

3363
02:08:18,800 --> 02:08:20,429
the dancers for each character.

3364
02:08:20,430 --> 02:08:21,699
It shows that you've really studied the character.

3365
02:08:21,700 --> 02:08:24,130
I was grateful that he recognized that.

3366
02:08:24,300 --> 02:08:25,440
But,

3367
02:08:25,800 --> 02:08:28,009
the tempo was too fast.

3368
02:08:28,010 --> 02:08:29,810
I understand because it was only a minute.

3369
02:08:30,340 --> 02:08:31,939
NaiN, Renan,

3370
02:08:31,940 --> 02:08:34,139
MIN JUN, then Hash...

3371
02:08:34,140 --> 02:08:35,650
(Non-stop switching between dancers)

3372
02:08:36,050 --> 02:08:37,149
It's fast.

3373
02:08:37,150 --> 02:08:39,619
If there had been even just a clear moment of rest,

3374
02:08:39,620 --> 02:08:42,720
it would have provided some breathing room and relief.

3375
02:08:42,990 --> 02:08:44,390
I don't know.

3376
02:08:44,560 --> 02:08:45,759
I can see that you've done...

3377
02:08:45,760 --> 02:08:48,589
a lot of analysis to bring the character to life.

3378
02:08:48,590 --> 02:08:51,459
But the background choreography...

3379
02:08:51,460 --> 02:08:54,829
was too "Hash-style."

3380
02:08:54,830 --> 02:08:56,629
What's wrong with "Hash-style?"

3381
02:08:56,630 --> 02:08:58,840
I was a bit frustrated.

3382
02:08:59,170 --> 02:09:00,869
The video we shot...

3383
02:09:00,870 --> 02:09:03,039
will continue to be played as the title sequence.

3384
02:09:03,040 --> 02:09:04,439
Taking that into account,

3385
02:09:04,440 --> 02:09:06,779
if the directors have a good sense for these things,

3386
02:09:06,780 --> 02:09:08,710
they'll choose mine.

3387
02:09:09,510 --> 02:09:12,019
Here we go.

3388
02:09:12,020 --> 02:09:15,589
I kept reminding myself that it was the opening video for the show.

3389
02:09:15,590 --> 02:09:18,319
So I wanted to properly shine a spotlight...

3390
02:09:18,320 --> 02:09:21,360
on each choreographer's character.

3391
02:09:21,790 --> 02:09:24,429
INGYOO and I thought exactly the same way.

3392
02:09:24,430 --> 02:09:25,899
(At the time of the concept presentation)

3393
02:09:25,900 --> 02:09:29,499
(They wanted to bring out the character of each choreographer.)

3394
02:09:29,500 --> 02:09:31,969
So that each person leaves a lasting impression to some extent.

3395
02:09:31,970 --> 02:09:35,440
I make a living by assigning parts.

3396
02:09:35,540 --> 02:09:37,910
I kept him somewhat in check.

3397
02:09:38,040 --> 02:09:40,479
Shall we look at the concept image? I have a few images.

3398
02:09:40,480 --> 02:09:44,109
I have improvised a setup inside the closed-down mart.

3399
02:09:44,110 --> 02:09:46,520
Hash is going to dance here.

3400
02:09:46,820 --> 02:09:48,219
(Me?)

3401
02:09:48,220 --> 02:09:50,149
"What?" I was taken aback.

3402
02:09:50,150 --> 02:09:51,219
Hash will show...

3403
02:09:51,220 --> 02:09:54,119
technique and character.

3404
02:09:54,120 --> 02:09:55,529
She'll run inside...

3405
02:09:55,530 --> 02:09:59,430
and people will catch her inside the tent.

3406
02:09:59,500 --> 02:10:03,229
He created a solo part by utilizing me.

3407
02:10:03,230 --> 02:10:04,699
It had a glamorous feel.

3408
02:10:04,700 --> 02:10:05,870
I was looking forward to it.

3409
02:10:06,200 --> 02:10:07,769
Next, it transitions to MIN JUN.

3410
02:10:07,770 --> 02:10:09,509
I'll use the space...

3411
02:10:09,510 --> 02:10:11,540
with the stairs for the first verse.

3412
02:10:11,780 --> 02:10:13,309
I'm looking forward to it.

3413
02:10:13,310 --> 02:10:15,810
I like that I have a role to play.

3414
02:10:15,850 --> 02:10:16,949
BADA will...

3415
02:10:16,950 --> 02:10:18,319
Simeez...

3416
02:10:18,320 --> 02:10:19,719
In case of Koo Young...

3417
02:10:19,720 --> 02:10:21,319
Do it in one take if possible...

3418
02:10:21,320 --> 02:10:23,749
It felt like each person was being shown...

3419
02:10:23,750 --> 02:10:25,459
and introduced..

3420
02:10:25,460 --> 02:10:27,959
In sync with the title sequence.

3421
02:10:27,960 --> 02:10:30,589
Perhaps it might help showcase my strengths...

3422
02:10:30,590 --> 02:10:33,229
in the first video.

3423
02:10:33,230 --> 02:10:34,770
Honestly, I was really tempted.

3424
02:10:35,270 --> 02:10:39,069
This is a draft for the Title Sequence Film Mission.

3425
02:10:39,070 --> 02:10:42,269
I am confident I can pull this off beautifully.

3426
02:10:42,270 --> 02:10:43,710
I think they'll be persuaded.

3427
02:10:44,070 --> 02:10:45,309
Just take a look.

3428
02:10:45,310 --> 02:10:46,809
Seeing is believing.

3429
02:10:46,810 --> 02:10:48,250
I'm really looking forward to it.

3430
02:10:48,650 --> 02:10:50,610
(Choreography Concept Credit Board, INGYOO)

3431
02:10:55,590 --> 02:10:57,450
The intro was really cool.

3432
02:11:00,060 --> 02:11:01,430
He gave her a solo part.

3433
02:11:02,190 --> 02:11:03,230
Hash.

3434
02:11:07,200 --> 02:11:08,699
If the parts are handled individually,

3435
02:11:08,700 --> 02:11:11,540
it can come across as loose to the viewer.

3436
02:11:14,440 --> 02:11:16,569
He used various staging elements for the solo part.

3437
02:11:16,570 --> 02:11:17,610
It was great.

3438
02:11:18,210 --> 02:11:19,880
What? It's Vata.

3439
02:11:20,510 --> 02:11:22,649
WE DEM BOYZ's distinct style...

3440
02:11:22,650 --> 02:11:24,749
really shone through.

3441
02:11:24,750 --> 02:11:26,250
It's the style I like.

3442
02:11:27,320 --> 02:11:29,790
The camera movement was really simple.

3443
02:11:33,420 --> 02:11:35,500
You absolutely have to use "get down on your knees."

3444
02:11:38,360 --> 02:11:39,930
- Me. - What? Look at that.

3445
02:11:40,200 --> 02:11:41,700
(Laughing)

3446
02:11:42,270 --> 02:11:44,230
It had a tribal vibe.

3447
02:11:44,470 --> 02:11:45,870
Impactful choreography.

3448
02:11:50,440 --> 02:11:52,110
Kamel is so good.

3449
02:11:52,180 --> 02:11:53,540
The choreography is good.

3450
02:11:54,080 --> 02:11:56,749
I don't think I can dance like Kamel.

3451
02:11:56,750 --> 02:11:58,050
